32 divisor)`) — 512 random triples PLUS hand-picked: divisor 0, exact division, rounding-half cases, negatives, values that overflow 32 bits, INT32_MIN. Log both the return code and `*res`.\n* L5 `png_reciprocal`, `png_reciprocal2` — random `png_fixed_point` values incl. 0, 1, -1, INT32_MIN/MAX.\n* L6 `png_gamma_significant`, `png_gamma_correct`, `png_gamma_8bit_correct`, `png_gamma_16bit_correct` — random gammas × random samples (8-bit: 0..255, 16-bit: 0..65535). `png_gamma_correct` takes a `png_structrp`. Note the C signatures use `unsigned int` for value and `png_fixed_point` for gamma.\n* L7 `png_XYZ_from_xy`, `png_xy_from_XYZ` — these take `png_XYZ*`/`png_xy*` structs: define matching `#[repr(C)]` structs in your file from `pngpriv.h` (each is 9 resp. 8 `png_fixed_point` fields — CHECK). Feed sRGB endpoints, random chromaticities, and degenerate zero cases; log return code and every output field.\n* L8 `png_check_fp_number`, `png_check_fp_string` — signatures in `pngpriv.h` (`png_check_fp_number(png_const_charp string, size_t size, int *statep, size_t *whereami)`). Cover: valid ints/floats/exponents, \"+.5e-3\", leading/trailing junk, empty, embedded NUL, strings of random ASCII (seeded), and start `*statep` at 0 as the C callers do.\n* L9 `png_ascii_from_fp`, `png_ascii_from_fixed` — `void png_ascii_from_fp(png_const_structrp, png_charp ascii, size_t size, double fp, unsigned int precision)`. Random doubles (incl. 0, ±tiny, ±huge, integral), precision 1..15, buffer sizes from tiny to 64. NOTE these call `png_error` when the buffer is too small — that is a Phase C row, so here use buffer sizes big enough (`PNG_FP_MAX_DIGITS`+ slack, e.g. 64) and log the written C string plus the whole buffer in hex.\n* L10 `png_fixed`, `png_fixed_ITU` — `png_fixed_point png_fixed(png_const_structrp png_ptr, double fp, png_const_charp text)`. Only in-range doubles here (out of range calls png_fixed_error → Phase C).\n* L11 `png_check_keyword` — signature in `pngpriv.h`. Random keywords + crafted: leading/trailing/multiple internal spaces, control chars (0x01..0x1f, 0x7f, 0x80..0x9f), >79 chars, empty, all-space. It writes into a `new_key[80]` buffer: log the returned length AND the full 80-byte buffer in hex AND all warnings produced (they are in the trace automatically).\n* L12 `png_safecat`, `png_format_number`, `png_warning_parameter`, `png_warning_parameter_unsigned`, `png_warning_parameter_signed`, `png_formatted_warning` — signatures in `pngpriv.h`. For the warning-parameter ones you need a `png_warning_parameters` array type: it is `char png_warning_parameters[PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_COUNT][PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_SIZE]` — get the two constants from `pngpriv.h` and declare an equivalent `#[repr(C)]` byte array. Exercise every `PNG_NUMBER_FORMAT_*` value, parameter numbers 1..count, oversized strings (truncation), and log the resulting formatted warning message text (it arrives through `cb_warning` into the trace).\n* L13 `png_build_grayscale_palette` — bit depths 1,2,4,8 and also 3 and 16 (the C writes nothing for those); pass a 256*3-byte buffer prefilled with 0xAA and log the whole buffer.\n* L14 `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer`, `png_convert_from_time_t`, `png_convert_from_struct_tm` — use the `PngTime` struct from `support::core`. Random times plus out-of-range fields (year 10000, month 0/13, day 0/32, hour 24, minute 60, second 61). For `png_convert_from_struct_tm` you need a `#[repr(C)] struct Tm` matching glibc `struct tm` (9 `c_int` fields, then `c_long tm_gmtoff`, `*const c_char tm_zone`). Log the return value and all output fields / the 29-byte buffer.\n* L15 `png_sig_cmp` — the correct 8-byte signature, every single-byte corruption of it, and all (start, num_to_check) pairs with start 0..9 and num 0..9.\n* L16 `png_calculate_crc`, `png_reset_crc`, `png_crc_error` — these need a read `png_struct`; they use `png_ptr->crc` / `chunk_name` internal state, so drive them as the C does: create a read struct, then for random buffers call `png_reset_crc`, `png_calculate_crc(png_ptr, data, len)` repeatedly, then `png_crc_error`. You cannot read `png_ptr->crc` directly, so make the observable be `png_crc_error()`'s return for a crafted expected-CRC — instead ALSO cover it end-to-end: use `pngbuild::crc32` to compute the true CRC, and additionally exercise `png_set_crc_action` with all 6×6 values on a valid stream (that part just must not diverge). Log every return value.\n* L17 `png_sRGB_table`, `png_sRGB_base`, `png_sRGB_delta` — exported DATA symbols. Use `lib.data(\"png_sRGB_table\")` etc. Sizes: `png_sRGB_table` is 256 `png_uint_16`, `png_sRGB_base` is 512 `png_uint_16`, `png_sRGB_delta` is 512 `png_byte` — VERIFY in `c_src/src/png.c`. Compare the full contents of both libraries.\n* L18 `png_malloc`, `png_calloc`, `png_malloc_warn`, `png_malloc_base`, `png_malloc_array`, `png_realloc_array`, `png_free`, `png_zalloc`, `png_zfree` — sizes 0, 1, 7, 1024, and a huge value (but for the huge/OOM cases only log the null-ness of the result, and remember `png_malloc` errors out on failure → that is Phase C; use `png_malloc_warn`/`png_malloc_base` for the failing sizes). Also drive them with a struct created by `png_create_read_struct_2` + the harness `cb_malloc`/`cb_free` and `with_session(|s| s.trace_alloc = true)` so the allocation sizes are compared. `png_malloc_array`/`png_realloc_array` signatures are in `pngpriv.h`.\n\nRULES (repeat of the important ones):\n* Fixed seeds everywhere; use `Rng::new(<literal>)`.\n* Never log pointer values — only null-ness, sizes and contents.\n* Do NOT edit anything except your new `tests/lowlevel_a.rs`. Never touch `src/`, `c_src/`,\n  `tests/support/*`, `Cargo.toml`.\n* If a test fails because the C and Rust traces genuinely differ, KEEP the test as-is and\n  report the divergence precisely (which function, which input, the two trace lines).\n  Do not `#[ignore]`, do not weaken, do not \"fix\" the Rust.\n* Compile+run with `timeout 600 cargo test --test lowlevel_a 2>&1 | tail -40`. Iterate until it\n  compiles cleanly. Fix your own test bugs (wrong signature, wrong buffer size, logging a\n  pointer, etc.).\n\nFINAL REPORT: list each test fn, whether it passes, and for every FAILING test the exact\ndivergence (C trace line vs Rust trace line, and the input that triggered it)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2466,"cache_read_input_tokens":173904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2466,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"275a5e39-d4cf-4e33-8dd0-7518fcdeddbb","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:15:12.100Z"}
