everal chunks\n  (`png_set_PLTE`, `png_set_tRNS`, `png_set_text`, `png_set_unknown_chunks`, `png_set_rows`),\n  then exercise `png_free_data` with each individual `PNG_FREE_*` mask and `PNG_FREE_ALL`,\n  `num` -1 and 0, and `png_data_freer` with DESTROY/SET/USER × masks; after each step log\n  `png_get_valid` for every flag and the getters for the affected chunks. Also\n  `png_info_init_3(&info, sizeof png_info)` — get the right size by comparing what the C\n  accepts: it warns/errors if the size differs, so use `png_create_info_struct` to obtain a\n  block and pass the correct `size_of` value (find `png_info` size handling in `pngset.c`/\n  `png.c`; the C compares against its own `sizeof(png_info)`), and also pass a deliberately\n  wrong size to see the identical message.\n* **L28** `png_check_IHDR(png_const_structrp, png_uint_32 width, png_uint_32 height, int bit_depth, int color_type, int interlace_type, int compression_type, int filter_type)`.\n  Call it DIRECTLY on a read struct for the full cross product: width {0,1,7,8,0x7fffffff,\n  0x80000000}, height {0,1,8}, bit_depth {0,1,2,3,4,7,8,16,32}, colour type {0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7},\n  interlace {0,1,2}, compression {0,1}, filter {0,1,64}. That is a lot — prune to a\n  deterministic random sample of ~400 combinations plus all 15 legal (colour,depth) pairs.\n  Every message (they are warnings/errors) lands in the trace; use `png_set_benign_errors(1)`\n  in one run and 0 in another. png_error longjmps, so structure the test as ONE\n  `diff`/`protected` run PER combination so an early exit does not hide later combinations.\n* **L29** `png_zstream_error`, `png_reset_zstream`, `png_inflate_claim`, `png_zlib_inflate`,\n  `png_inflate` — read the C in `c_src/src/pngrutil.c`. Drive them through real inflate work:\n  build PNGs whose IDAT/zTXt/iCCP zlib streams are (a) valid stored-deflate,\n  (b) valid multi-block, (c) truncated, (d) with a bad adler32, (e) with an invalid CMF byte,\n  using `pngbuild::zlib_stored` and hand-