{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Np91Ba2HBK5Wy3biajLX9E","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Differential-test harness — how to write a test file\n2\t\n3\tCrate: `translated_rust` (libpng 1.6.59 C→Rust). Working dir for all commands:\n4\t`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust`.\n5\t\n6\tThe C reference `.so` is `target/cbuild/libpng.so`; the Rust `.so` is\n7\t`target/debug/liblibpng.so`. **Both are loaded with `libloading`** and every\n8\tlibpng call goes through `dlsym`. Never call the Rust crate directly.\n9\t\n10\t## Skeleton of a test file (`tests/<group>.rs`)\n11\t\n12\t```rust\n13\t//! <group> differential tests (CONFIGS.md rows Xn..Xm)\n14\tmod support;\n15\t\n16\tuse std::ffi::{c_char, c_int, c_void};\n17\tuse support::core::*;\n18\tuse support::*;\n19\t\n20\t#[test]\n21\tfn r1_read_all_colour_types() {\n22\t    for &(ct, bd) in COMBOS {\n23\t        let png_bytes = /* build input, identical for both libs */;\n24\t        diff(&format!(\"R1 ct={ct} bd={bd}\"), |lib| {\n25\t            with_read(lib, &png_bytes, &mut |c, png, info| unsafe {\n26\t                (c.read_info)(png, info);\n27\t                log_all_info(c, png, info);\n28\t                /* ... rows ... */\n29\t                (c.read_end)(png, std::ptr::null_mut());\n30\t            })\n31\t        });\n32\t    }\n33\t}\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\t`diff(label, f)` runs `f` once with the C `Lib` and once with the Rust `Lib` and\n37\tpanics if the two traces differ (it prints the first differing trace line).\n38\t\n39\t## The API surface\n40\t\n41\t`support::core::Core::new(lib)` resolves ~200 typed function pointers\n42\t(`c.read_info`, `c.set_IHDR`, `c.write_row`, ...). Read\n43\t`tests/support/core.rs` for the exact field names/signatures — they mirror\n44\t`png.h` names with the `png_` prefix removed. It also defines all the\n45\t`PNG_*` constants, `PngColor16`, `PngColor8`, `PngTime`, `PngText`,\n46\t`PngUnknownChunk`, `PngSpltT`, `PngSpltEntry`, `PngImage`, `PngRowInfo`\n47\t(`#[repr(C)]`, verified against `png.h`).\n48\t\n49\tAnything not in `Core` is fetched ad hoc, e.g.\n50\t\n51\t```rust\n52\tlet muldiv: unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut i32, i32, i32, i32) -> c_int = lib.f(\"png_muldiv\");\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\tSignatures MUST be taken from `c_src/include/png.h` / `c_src/include/pngpriv.h`.\n56\tMap: `png_uint_32`→`u32`, `png_int_32`/`png_fixed_point`→`i32`, `png_byte`→`u8`,\n57\t`png_uint_16`→`u16`, `size_t`→`usize`, `int`→`c_int`, `double`→`f64`,\n58\t`png_structrp`/`png_structp`/`png_const_structrp`→`Png` (= `*mut c_void`),\n59\t`png_inforp`→`Info`, `png_bytep`→`*mut u8`, `png_const_bytep`→`*const u8`,\n60\t`png_charp`→`*mut c_char`, callback pointers→`Cb` (= `*mut c_void`, pass\n61\t`my_cb as Cb`).\n62\t\n63\t## Helpers you must use\n64\t\n65\t* `with_write(lib, &mut |c, png, info| { ... }) -> Trace` — creates a write\n66\t  struct with the harness error/warning/write/flush callbacks and a longjmp\n67\t  landing pad, runs the body, destroys the struct. The produced bytes end up in\n68\t  `Trace::out`.\n69\t* `with_read(lib, input_bytes, &mut |c, png, info| { ... }) -> Trace` — same for\n70\t  reading; the read callback serves `input_bytes`.\n71\t* `protected(|| ...) -> c_int` — raw setjmp landing pad, for tests that build\n72\t  their own structs (e.g. `png_create_read_struct_2`). Returns 0 on normal\n73\t  completion, non-zero if libpng longjmp'ed. **Anything after a `png_error` is\n74\t  not executed**, so put the trace-relevant calls before it.\n75\t* `log(...)` — append a line to the trace. Everything you want compared must be\n76\t  logged.\n77\t* `log_all_info(c, png, info)` — logs every ancillary-chunk getter result.\n78\t* `hex(&[u8])` — hex string of a byte slice (use it to log rows/buffers).\n79\t* `cstr(*const c_char)` — safe C string → `String` (logs `<null>` for NULL).\n80\t* `Rng::new(seed)` — deterministic xorshift PRNG: `next_u32`, `below(n)`,\n81\t  `byte()`, `bytes(n)`, `f64()`. **Every test must use a fixed seed.**\n82\t* `with_session(|s| ...)` — access the session: `s.trace_alloc = true` (log\n83\t  every user-memory malloc/free size), `s.malloc_limit = Some(n)` (fail malloc\n84\t  after n allocations), `s.write_limit`, `s.input`, `s.rpos`.\n85\t* `support::pngbuild` — build/dissect PNG datastreams without either library:\n86\t  `Builder::new(w,h,depth,color).interlace(1).add(b\"gAMA\", data).build_valid(seed)`,\n87\t  `zlib_stored(&raw)`, `Chunk::new(b\"tEXt\", data).bad_crc()`, `split(png)`,\n88\t  `join(&chunks)`, `rowbytes()`, `pass_width/pass_height`, `crc32`, `adler32`.\n89\t* Callbacks provided by the harness (pass as `Cb`): `cb_error`, `cb_warning`,\n90\t  `cb_read`, `cb_write`, `cb_flush`, `cb_malloc`, `cb_free`.\n91\t* `shim().longjmp_ptr` / `shim().jmp_buf_size` for `png_set_longjmp_fn`.\n92\t\n93\t## Hard rules\n94\t\n95\t1. **NEVER log a pointer value, address, or anything else that legitimately\n96\t   differs between two independent libraries.** Log only null-ness, sizes,\n97\t   contents. (`log_all_info` already follows this rule.)\n98\t2. **NEVER weaken a test to make it pass.** If the C and Rust traces differ,\n99\t   that is either (a) a bug in your test/harness use, or (b) a genuine\n100\t   translation bug. Investigate; if it is (b), leave the test in place and\n101\t   REPORT it — do not `#[ignore]` it, do not relax the assertion, and do not\n102\t   edit anything in `src/` or `c_src/`.\n103\t3. Use several randomized inputs per configuration (a loop over 8..64 seeds or\n104\t   shapes), not one hand-picked value.\n105\t4. Keep individual test functions fast (whole file well under 60 s). Images of\n106\t   1..40 pixels per side are plenty; a few larger ones are fine.\n107\t5. Closures passed to `protected`/`with_*` must not own values needing `Drop`\n108\t   (a `png_error` longjmp skips destructors). Allocate `Vec`s *outside* the\n109\t   closure and use raw pointers/slices inside.\n110\t6. `libpng` writes into caller buffers: always allocate `rowbytes+8` slack and\n111\t   compare exactly what the C wrote (log the whole buffer).\n112\t7. Rows are read into buffers you own; for `png_read_row(png, row, display)` you\n113\t   may pass NULL for either but not both.\n114\t8. Only ONE `mod support;` per test file; use `#[test]` functions.\n115\t\n116\t## Running\n117\t\n118\t```bash\n119\tcd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust\n120\ttimeout 600 cargo test --test <group> 2>&1 | tail -40\n121\t# a single test:\n122\ttimeout 600 cargo test --test <group> <fn_name> -- --nocapture 2>&1 | tail -40\n123\t```\n124\t\n125\tIf `target/cbuild/libpng.so` is missing:\n126\t\n127\t```bash\n128\tcmake -S c_src -B target/cbuild -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON && cmake --build target/cbuild -j8\n129\t```\n130\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KKgwxwravRomJENipvomj6","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"95cd5694-b457-4a02-b433-65366ba47eaf","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:16:08.722Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lowlevel_b tests L19-L29"}
