{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uss7s7rsqa2rg5rb26uj555fu4b3jkq2ob5fxoisthmjnl7lgula","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01XGJhK7CyRFH4G9gHb8xDNT","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write chunk round-trip tests C1-C24","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration test file for a C→Rust differential verification of libpng 1.6.59.\n\nWorking dir: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust`\n\nFIRST read (short): `tests/HARNESS.md`, `tests/support/core.rs`, `tests/smoke.rs`, and the \"C\"\nsection of `CONFIGS.md`. You implement rows **C1 through C24**.\n\nCREATE exactly one new file: `tests/chunks.rs`, one `#[test]` fn per row (`c1_...` … `c24_...`).\nEvery test drives BOTH `.so`s with `diff(...)` and compares the full trace byte-for-byte.\n\nThe pattern for a chunk row is a full ROUND TRIP, because that exercises `pngset.c`,\n`pngwutil.c`, `pngrutil.c` and `pngget.c` together:\n\n```\n// 1. WRITE: with_write(...) -> set_IHDR, set_<CHUNK>(...), write_info, rows, write_end\n//    (log the setter's observable effects: png_get_valid + the matching getter)\n// 2. the produced bytes are in Trace::out -- but you cannot use them across the\n//    two libraries directly. Instead: do the whole write+read INSIDE one `diff`\n//    closure, i.e. write with `lib`, then feed the bytes you just produced back\n//    into a read with the SAME `lib`, and log everything. The two libraries then\n//    each produce a complete write+read trace which must be identical.\n```\n\nConcretely, inside the `diff` closure do:\n\n```rust\nlet t1 = with_write(lib, &mut |c, png, info| unsafe { ...set chunk..., write_info, rows, write_end });\nlet produced = t1.out.clone();\nlet mut lines = t1.lines.clone();\nlet t2 = with_read(lib, &produced, &mut |c, png, info| unsafe {\n    (c.read_info)(png, info);\n    log_all_info(c, png, info);\n    /* read all rows */\n    (c.read_end)(png, info);   // end info: use a second info struct where relevant\n    log_all_info(c, png, info);\n});\nlines.extend(t2.lines);\nTrace { lines, out: produced, rc: t1.rc | (t2.rc << 8) }\n```\n(`log_all_info` already logs every ancillary getter, so most of the comparison is free.)\n\nRows (use the EXACT signatures from `c_src/include/png.h`; `Core` already has most of them):\n\n* **C1** `png_set_PLTE`/`png_get_PLTE`: 1, 2, 16, 255, 256 entries × palette bit depths 1/2/4/8\n  (only legal sizes for the depth), plus a palette attached to an RGB (colour type 2) image\n  (legal, written as a suggested palette).\n* **C2** `png_set_tRNS`/`png_get_tRNS`: palette alpha arrays of 1..256 entries; grey key\n  (colour 0, 8 and 16 bit); RGB key (colour 2, 8 and 16 bit) — use `PngColor16`.\n* **C3** `png_set_gAMA` (double) and `png_set_gAMA_fixed` (png_fixed_point) + both getters:\n  random gammas in the legal range, plus 1, 100000, 45455, 220000, and the values right at the\n  limits the C accepts (out-of-range values that produce a warning are fine to include ONLY if\n  the warning text is identical in both — keep them, they are legitimate valid-API calls).\n* **C4** `png_set_sRGB` and `png_set_sRGB_gAMA_and_cHRM` with intent 0..3.\n* **C5** `png_set_cHRM`, `png_set_cHRM_fixed`, `png_set_cHRM_XYZ`, `png_set_cHRM_XYZ_fixed`\n  + `png_get_cHRM*`: sRGB primaries, random plausible chromaticities, XYZ round trip.\n* **C6** `png_set_iCCP`/`png_get_iCCP`: synthetic ICC profiles that pass libpng's checks.\n  Read `png_icc_check_header`/`png_icc_check_length`/`png_icc_check_tag_table` in\n  `c_src/src/png.c` and build a minimal VALID profile (132-byte header + tag table with 0 or a\n  few tags, correct size field, 'acsp' signature, valid colour space / PCS / rendering intent,\n  correct padding). Sizes 132..2048, keyword lengths 1..79. Log the profile bytes back from\n  `png_get_iCCP`.\n* **C7** `png_set_sBIT`/getter: every colour type with legal sBIT values (1..bit_depth per\n  channel) using `PngColor8`.\n* **C8** `png_set_bKGD`/getter: palette index, grey, RGB, 16-bit (`PngColor16`).\n* **C9** `png_set_hIST`/getter: palette sizes 2, 16, 256 with random `u16` frequencies.\n* **C10** `png_set_pHYs`/`png_get_pHYs` + `png_get_pHYs_dpi`, `png_get_x_pixels_per_meter`,\n  `png_get_y_pixels_per_meter`, `png_get_x_pixels_per_inch`, `png_get_y_pixels_per_inch`,\n  `png_get_pixels_per_inch`, `png_get_pixel_aspect_ratio`, `png_get_pixel_aspect_ratio_fixed`:\n  random resolutions × unit 0/1 (resolve these extra getters with `lib.f(...)`; log the\n  floating-point results with `{:.10}` so tiny differences show).\n* **C11** `png_set_oFFs`/`png_get_oFFs` + `png_get_x_offset_pixels`, `png_get_y_offset_pixels`,\n  `png_get_x_offset_microns`, `png_get_y_offset_microns`, `png_get_x_offset_inches`,\n  `png_get_y_offset_inches` (+ `_fixed`): negative and positive offsets × unit 0/1.\n* **C12** `png_set_tIME`/getter + `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` on the value read back:\n  random times, plus field extremes.\n* **C13** `png_set_pCAL`/`png_get_pCAL`: equation type 0..3, nparams 0..3, random ASCII\n  parameter strings (the C parses them as floating point — include integers, decimals and\n  exponents), purposes/units with 8-bit characters.\n* **C14** `png_set_sCAL` (double), `png_set_sCAL_fixed`, `png_set_sCAL_s` (strings) +\n  `png_get_sCAL`, `png_get_sCAL_fixed`, `png_get_sCAL_s`: unit 1 and 2, random positive\n  dimensions in all three forms.\n* **C15** `png_set_sPLT`/`png_get_sPLT`: 1..3 palettes, depth 8 and 16, 1..16 entries\n  (`PngSpltT` + `PngSpltEntry` from `support::core`), names with internal spaces.\n* **C16** `png_set_eXIf_1`/`png_get_eXIf_1`: random EXIF blobs starting with \"II*\\0\" and\n  \"MM\\0*\", lengths 4..1024. (`png_set_eXIf` is the deprecated variant — cover it too if its\n  behaviour is well-defined in this version: read `png_set_eXIf` in `pngset.c` first.)\n* **C17** `png_set_cICP`/getter: random primaries/transfer/matrix (matrix 0 is the value libpng\n  accepts — check `pngset.c`)/full-range flag.\n* **C18** `png_set_cLLI` (float) and `png_set_cLLI_fixed` + getters: random maxCLL/maxFALL\n  incl. 0.\n* **C19** `png_set_mDCV` (float) and `png_set_mDCV_fixed` + getters: random display primaries,\n  white point, max/min luminance.\n* **C20** `png_set_text`/`png_get_text`: 1..8 entries mixing `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_NONE`\n  (tEXt), `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt`, `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_NONE`,\n  `PNG_ITXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt`; empty text, text with 8-bit characters, NULL `text` pointer,\n  `lang`/`lang_key` set and NULL (use `PngText` from `support::core`, keep the CString buffers\n  alive outside the closure).\n* **C21** `png_set_unknown_chunks` + `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` + `png_get_unknown_chunks`\n  (+ `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` on the read side so they survive): 1..4 chunks with\n  private-but-legal names (lowercase 3rd letter is reserved — use names like `b\"prVt\"`,\n  `b\"teSt\"`), 0-length data, locations before-PLTE / before-IDAT / after-IDAT.\n* **C22** `png_set_rows`/`png_get_rows` + `png_write_png`/`png_read_png` round trip\n  (`PNG_TRANSFORM_IDENTITY`), then `png_free_data(png, info, PNG_FREE_ROWS, -1)`.\n* **C23** `png_set_invalid` + `png_get_valid`: set every chunk, then invalidate each\n  `PNG_INFO_*` flag one at a time and log all flags after each step.\n* **C24** ONE image carrying EVERY supported ancillary chunk at once (gAMA, cHRM, sRGB *or*\n  iCCP — note the C warns when both are set, keep whichever combination is legal and also test\n  the warning case since it is a legitimate API sequence —, sBIT, bKGD, hIST, pHYs, oFFs, tIME,\n  pCAL, sCAL, sPLT, eXIf, cICP, cLLI, mDCV, tEXt+zTXt+iTXt, tRNS, PLTE, unknown chunks),\n  written, then read back with everything logged; run it for a palette image and for an RGBA\n  16-bit image.\n\nRULES:\n* Fixed seeds only (`Rng::new(<literal>)`).\n* Never log a pointer/address — only null-ness, sizes, contents.\n* Keep all `CString`/`Vec` backing buffers ALIVE outside the `protected` closure (a longjmp\n  skips destructors; also libpng only copies what it documents as copied).\n* Do NOT edit anything except your new `tests/chunks.rs`. Never touch `src/`, `c_src/`,\n  `tests/support/*`, `Cargo.toml`, or other test files.\n* If C and Rust genuinely diverge: KEEP the test, do NOT weaken it, do NOT `#[ignore]`, do NOT\n  modify `src/`. Report it precisely.\n* Run `timeout 600 cargo test --test chunks 2>&1 | tail -40`; iterate until it compiles and only\n  genuine divergences remain. Keep runtime under ~90 s (small images: 8x4 is plenty).\n\nFINAL REPORT: per test fn — pass/fail, and for each failure the exact C-vs-Rust trace\ndifference plus the triggering configuration."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":772,"cache_read_input_tokens":191588,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":772,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"be221cc9-255c-44e1-954d-f773aab95486","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:18:33.894Z"}
