info);\n    log_all_info(c, png_ptr, info);\n    let rb = (c.get_rowbytes)(png_ptr, info);\n    log(format!(\"rowbytes_after_update={rb} channels={}\", (c.get_channels)(png_ptr, info)));\n    for r in 0..h { (c.read_row)(png_ptr, buf.as_mut_ptr(), std::ptr::null_mut());\n                    log(format!(\"row{r}={}\", hex(&buf[..rb]))); }\n    (c.read_end)(png_ptr, std::ptr::null_mut());\n})\n```\nAllocate row buffers with generous slack (e.g. `rb_max + 16`) and log exactly `rb` bytes plus,\nseparately, the slack bytes so a buffer overrun in either library is visible.\n\nRows:\n* **R1** no transforms: all 15 combos × interlace 0 and 1 × widths 1,3,7,8,17 × heights 1,5.\n  For interlaced input call `png_set_interlace_handling` and read pass by pass.\n* **R2** `png_read_rows(png, row_pointers, display_row_pointers, num_rows)`: num_rows 1 and all;\n  with `row` only, with `display_row` only, and with both (all three are legal).\n* **R3** `png_read_image(png, row_pointers)`: all combos × interlace 0/1.\n* **R4** `png_read_png(png, info, transforms, NULL)`: every `PNG_TRANSFORM_*` bit that\n  `png_read_png` honours (read `png_read_png` in `c_src/src/pngread.c`) individually plus 8\n  seeded random combinations; log the rows via `png_get_rows` afterwards.\n* **R5** `png_set_interlace_handling` + row-by-row on Adam7 input, all 7 passes, every combo.\n* **R6** `png_set_packing`: GRAY and PALETTE at 1, 2, 4 bits.\n* **R7** `png_set_packswap`: GRAY and PALETTE at 1, 2, 4 bits (also combined with packing).\n* **R8** `png_set_expand`: on palette input (→RGB), on GRAY < 8 bit (→8 bit), and on input with a\n  tRNS chunk (→alpha). Build one input for each triggering condition, and also apply\n  `png_set_expand` where nothing needs expanding.\n* **R9** `png_set_expand_16`: every colour type at 8 bit (and at 1/2/4 bit combined with\n  `png_set_expand`).\n* **R10** `png_set_expand_gray_1_2_4_to_8`, `png_set_palette_to_rgb`, `png_set_tRNS_to_alpha`\n  individually, each on a matching input AND on a non-matching colour type (the C simply does\n  nothing or warns — the trace must match either way).\n* **R11** `png_set_gray_to_rgb`: GRAY and GRAY_ALPHA at 1,2,4,8,16 bit.\n* **R12** `png_set_rgb_to_gray` (double) and `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed`: error_action 1,2,3 ×\n  (red,green) coefficient pairs {(-1,-1) default, (0.2125,0.7154), (0.5,0.5), (0,0), (1,0)} ×\n  RGB and RGB_ALPHA at 8 and 16 bit; log `png_get_rgb_to_gray_status` after every row. Include\n  input rows that are NOT grey (so error_action 2/3 triggers its message) and rows that ARE grey.\n* **R13** `png_set_strip_16` and `png_set_scale_16` on 16-bit input of every colour type.\n* **R14** `png_set_strip_alpha` on GRAY_ALPHA and RGB_ALPHA at 8 and 16 bit.\n* **R15** `png_set_filler` and `png_set_add_alpha` with `PNG_FILLER_BEFORE` and\n  `PNG_FILLER_AFTER` × filler values {0, 0x7f, 0xff, 0xffff, 0x1234} × GRAY and RGB at 8 and\n  16 bit (and, for `png_set_add_alpha`, also on inputs that already have alpha).\n* **R16** `png_set_swap`, `png_set_bgr`, `png_set_invert_mono`, `png_set_invert_alpha`,\n  `png_set_swap_alpha`: each alone on every applicable colour type/depth, plus the pairwise\n  combinations that apply (e.g. swap+bgr on RGB 16-bit, invert_alpha+swap_alpha on RGBA).\n\nRULES:\n* Fixed seeds only (`Rng::new(<literal>)`); several inputs per configuration.\n* Never log a pointer/address — only null-ness, sizes, contents.\n* Do NOT edit anything except your new `tests/read_a.rs`. Never touch `src/`, `c_src/`,\n  `tests/support/*`, `Cargo.toml`, or other test files.\n* If C and Rust genuinely diverge: KEEP the test, do NOT weaken it, do NOT `#[ignore]`, do NOT\n  modify `src/`. Report it precisely (row number, configuration, the two trace lines).\n* Run `timeout 600 cargo test --test read_a 2>&1 | tail -40`; iterate until it compiles and only\n  genuine divergences remain. Keep runtime under ~90 s (images ≤ 17×8).\n\nFINAL REPORT: per test fn — pass/fail, and for each failure the exact C-vs-Rust trace\ndifference plus the triggering configuration.","uuid":"83a58ca7-dd1c-4252-b42e-b4e9e8b10d69","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e"}
