`, `GRAY_TO_RGB`, …) are silently ignored, not warned about. Kept away from Phase C: `png_set_filler` is only exercised on RGB and GRAY≥8 (other colour types are an app error, `pngtrans.c:208-212`), `BEFORE|AFTER` together is masked out, and `SHIFT` always has a valid sBIT (values `max(1,bd-1)`) so `png_set_shift`'s range check passes.\n- **W12 clamp correction** — the task brief says \"the C clamps 8→9 with a warning\". That is not what 1.6.59 does: `png_set_compression_window_bits` (`pngwrite.c:1254-1280`) clamps `<8 → 8` (\"Only compression windows >= 256 supported by PNG\") and `>15 → 15` (\"Only compression windows <= 32k supported by PNG\"); windowBits 8 is passed to `deflateInit2` unchanged (zlib itself treats it as 9, silently). To still cover the warning path I added `window_bits ∈ {7, 16}` alongside `{8,9,10,15}`, and the test asserts the warning is present iff `wb ∉ [8,15]` — it fires identically in both libraries.\n- Also compared per configuration: `png_get_rowbytes`, `png_get_channels`, `png_get_compression_buffer_size` (before and after `png_write_png`), `png_set_interlace_handling`'s pass count, `png_get_valid(PLTE/tRNS/IDAT/sBIT)`, `png_get_rows` null-ness, and a CRC over all caller row buffers (`rowsum=`) proving neither library mutates the application's rows.\n- Every driver is guarded by `checked()`: `rc == 0` and the output must start with the PNG signature, so no configuration can silently pass by doing nothing. I verified the comparison actually bites by temporarily flipping one output bit in the Rust run — all 12 tests then failed with `out=` divergences; the instrumentation was removed afterwards.\n\n### Unrelated\n`cargo test` (whole workspace) currently fails in **`tests/lowlevel_a.rs`**, a file created by another concurrent agent — outside my scope; `cargo test --test write_a` and `--test smoke` are green."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":551,"cache_read