{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"aa93674a3b9b8d64d","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012LCvo8bjj71evPUNPs2Hr6","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-4DaaTZ-translated-rust/11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e/tasks/aa93674a3b9b8d64d.output","summary":"Done. `tests/lowlevel_a.rs` created (only new file; nothing else touched).\n\n## Result: 17 of 18 pass, 1 genuine divergence\n\n```\ntimeout 600 cargo test --test lowlevel_a    →   17 passed; 1 failed   (0.13 s)\n```\n\n| test fn | row | status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `l1_get_uint_and_int` | L1 | PASS |\n| `l2_get_uint_31_valid` | L2 | PASS |\n| `l3_save_uint_and_int` | L3 | PASS |\n| `l4_muldiv` | L4 | PASS |\n| `l5_reciprocal` | L5 | PASS |\n| `l6_gamma_helpers` | L6 | **FAIL** |\n| `l7_xyz_xy_conversions` | L7 | PASS |\n| `l8_check_fp_number_and_string` | L8 | PASS |\n| `l9_ascii_from_fp_and_fixed` | L9 | PASS |\n| `l10_png_fixed` | L10 | PASS |\n| `l11_check_keyword` | L11 | PASS |\n| `l12_string_and_warning_helpers` | L12 | PASS |\n| `l13_build_grayscale_palette` | L13 | PASS |\n| `l14_time_conversions` | L14 | PASS |\n| `l15_sig_cmp` | L15 | PASS |\n| `l16_crc` | L16 | PASS |\n| `l17_srgb_tables` | L17 | PASS |\n| `l18_memory` | L18 | PASS |\n\n## The divergence (L6 — real translation bug)\n\n```\n[L6 pure] C and Rust diverge\nfirst divergence at trace line 129:\n  C   : L6 g16[2] v=1 g=-1 -> 6\n  RUST: L6 g16[2] v=1 g=-1 -> 65535\n```\nInput: `png_gamma_16bit_correct(value = 1, gamma_value = -1)`.\n\nRoot cause — **saturating vs. truncating `double`→integer cast**. Both implementations compute the same `double`\n`r = floor(65535*pow(1/65535., -1e-5)+.5) == 65542.0`, then:\n* `c_src/src/png.c` `return (png_uint_16)r;` → x86-64 gcc truncates: `65542 & 0xffff == 6`\n* `src/png.rs:2230` `return r as png_uint_16;` → Rust `as` **saturates**: `65535`\n\nIndependently confirmed (ctypes probe against both `.so`s) that this affects a family of inputs, and the identical bug exists in `png_gamma_8bit_correct` (`src/png.rs`, `r as png_byte`), and therefore in `png_gamma_correct`, which dispatches to both:\n\n| call | C | Rust |\n|---|---|---|\n| `png_gamma_16bit_correct(1, -1)` | 6 | 65535 |\n| `png_gamma_16bit_correct(127, -1)` | 3 | 65535 |\n| `png_gamma_16bit_correct(65534, INT32_MIN)` | 25411 | 65535 |\n| `png_gamma_16bit_correct(1, INT32_MIN)` | 0 | 65535 |\n| `png_gamma_8bit_correct(1, INT32_MIN)` | 0 | 255 |\n| `png_gamma_8bit_correct(254, INT32_MIN)` | 0 | 255 |\n\nReachable whenever `65535*pow(v/65535., gamma*1e-5)` exceeds 65535 (resp. 255), i.e. for gamma values below 0 or otherwise out of the sane range. Test left in place, unmodified, not `#[ignore]`d.\n\n## Notes for the harness owner\n\n* `target/cbuild/libpng.so` is **linked without `-lm`** (`nm -D -u` shows undefined `floor` and `pow`; `readelf -d` lists only `libz.so.1`/`libc.so.6`). Any test that reaches libpng's floating-point paths dies with `symbol lookup error: … undefined symbol: floor`. Worked around test-side in `ensure_libm()` (dlopens `libm.so.6` with `RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL`, identically for both libraries); the real fix belongs in the cmake invocation. Rows L6/L9/L10 all need it.\n* `png_crc_error` is `static` in `c_src/src/pngrutil.c` and is **not an exported symbol in either `.so`**, so it cannot be called through `dlsym`. L16 therefore uses `png_crc_finish` (exported) as the observable, driving `png_reset_crc`/`png_calculate_crc` exactly as `png_crc_read` does, with the stream serving a true CRC, a corrupted CRC, and a `skip`-driven read, plus all 6×6 `png_set_crc_action` pairs over a valid stream, a bad-ancillary-CRC stream and a bad-critical-CRC stream.\n* `Core::get_uint_16` is declared `-> c_uint` but the C function returns `png_uint_16`; the upper 16 bits of `eax` are unspecified on return. L1 resolves its own `-> u16` pointer instead.\n* L18 resets `Session::malloc_count` and only turns on `trace_alloc` *after* `png_create_read_struct_2` + `png_set_longjmp_fn`, since `sizeof(png_struct)` and the internal jmp_buf allocation legitimately differ between the two libraries.","usage":{"total_tokens":190846,"tool_uses":79,"duration_ms":978549},"uuid":"dc3d6f18-cfbd-4192-828f-4c95060a3b62","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e"}
