{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6qd6wj4mhdu2ejl4pekcbgnisnbfounqr7h5prjnkb3ke63bylsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_0142wgcwC4DU2gkmXGMTmwBC","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write write_b tests W13-W24","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration test file for a C→Rust differential verification of libpng 1.6.59.\n\nWorking dir: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust`\n\nFIRST read (short): `tests/HARNESS.md`, `tests/support/core.rs`, `tests/write_a.rs` (an existing,\nfully passing example of exactly this kind of file — copy its style), and the \"W\" section of\n`CONFIGS.md`. You implement rows **W13 through W24 only**.\n\nCREATE exactly one new file: `tests/write_b.rs`, one `#[test]` fn per row (`w13_...` … `w24_...`).\nEvery test drives BOTH `.so`s with `diff(...)` and compares the produced PNG byte stream and the\nwhole trace byte-for-byte.\n\n* **W13** `png_set_compression_method` (only 8 is legal; other values produce a specific message →\n  that belongs to Phase C, so use 8) and `png_set_compression_buffer_size` with sizes\n  1, 2, 3, 100, 1024, 8192, 65536 on an image whose IDAT is much larger than the buffer, so\n  `png_compress_IDAT` has to emit multiple IDAT chunks. Log `png_get_compression_buffer_size`.\n  Also cover setting the buffer size AFTER `png_write_info` (legal, read the C to see what it does).\n* **W14** `png_set_flush(n)` for n = 0, 1, 2, 3, 7 plus explicit `png_write_flush` calls between\n  rows; the harness `cb_flush` logs `FLUSH` into the trace, so the flush *ordering* relative to\n  the produced bytes is compared. Use ≥ 10 rows.\n* **W15** `png_write_sig`, `png_write_chunk`, `png_write_chunk_start` + `png_write_chunk_data`\n  (called several times) + `png_write_chunk_end`: random 4-byte chunk names that are legal\n  private/ancillary names, payload lengths 0, 1, 13, 1000; interleaved with a normal\n  write_info/rows/write_end sequence (write the extra chunks after `png_write_info` and after the\n  rows, which is what applications do).\n* **W16** `png_write_info_before_PLTE` followed by `png_write_info`, on a palette image with\n  PLTE + tRNS + several ancillary chunks (gAMA, sBIT, bKGD, hIST, pHYs, tEXt), and on an RGB\n  image; also the sequence where only `png_write_info` is called (the C calls\n  `png_write_info_before_PLTE` internally).\n* **W17** write transforms: `png_set_bgr`, `png_set_swap`, `png_set_packswap`,\n  `png_set_invert_mono`, `png_set_invert_alpha`, `png_set_swap_alpha`,\n  `png_set_filler(value, PNG_FILLER_BEFORE|AFTER)`, `png_set_shift(&PngColor8)`,\n  `png_set_packing`. Apply each ALONE on every colour type/bit depth where the C accepts it\n  (read `c_src/src/pngtrans.c` + `c_src/src/pngwtran.c` to see which combinations are accepted —\n  e.g. `png_set_filler` on a colour type without the right channel count is an app error, which\n  is a Phase C row and must NOT be used here), then 8 seeded random combinations of the\n  compatible ones. For `png_set_shift` the image must have a valid sBIT (`png_set_sBIT` with\n  values in 1..bit_depth).\n* **W18** `png_set_write_user_transform_fn` + `png_set_user_transform_info`: write an\n  `unsafe extern \"C\" fn(png_ptr: Png, row_info: *mut PngRowInfo, data: *mut u8)` callback that\n  (a) logs the row_info fields and the row bytes and (b) deterministically rewrites the row\n  (e.g. XOR each byte with its index). Cover several colour types/depths and interlace 0/1, and\n  `png_set_user_transform_info(png, ptr, depth, channels)` with values matching and (legally)\n  differing from the image; log `png_get_user_transform_ptr`.\n* **W19** `png_set_write_status_fn`: callback\n  `unsafe extern \"C\" fn(Png, u32 /*row*/, c_int /*pass*/)` that logs (row, pass); interlace 0\n  and 1, all four write APIs (`write_row`, `write_rows`, `write_image`, `write_png`).\n* **W20** `png_set_text` on the WRITE side with `png_set_text_compression_level` ∈ {0,1,6,9},\n  `png_set_text_compression_strategy` ∈ {0,1,2,3,4}, `png_set_text_compression_window_bits`\n  ∈ {9,12,15}, `png_set_text_compression_mem_level` ∈ {1,8}: tEXt, zTXt and iTXt entries\n  (compressed and uncompressed, with and without lang/lang_key), text long enough to compress\n  (≥ 500 bytes, repetitive). Keep the `CString` buffers alive outside the closure.\n* **W21** `png_write_end(png, end_info)` where `end_info` is a SECOND info struct carrying tIME\n  and text chunks (chunks after IDAT), and `png_write_end(png, NULL)`.\n* **W22** 16-bit images + `png_set_swap` + interlace 0/1 + `png_set_filter` with each filter and\n  ALL filters, ≥ 12 rows of data with structure (so the filter heuristic makes real choices).\n  Colour types 0, 2, 4, 6 at bit depth 16.\n* **W23** `png_create_write_struct_2(ver, err_ptr, cb_error, cb_warning, mem_ptr, cb_malloc, cb_free)`:\n  do a complete write through the harness user-memory callbacks with\n  `with_session(|s| s.trace_alloc = true)` so every allocation SIZE and order is compared.\n  IMPORTANT: turn `trace_alloc` on only AFTER `png_create_write_struct_2` and\n  `png_set_longjmp_fn` (the size of `png_struct` itself legitimately differs between the two\n  libraries; the sizes libpng asks for afterwards must not). Also log `png_get_mem_ptr`\n  null-ness and `png_get_error_ptr` null-ness. Cover 4 colour types × interlace 0/1.\n  Follow the pattern in `tests/lowlevel_a.rs` fn `l18_memory` (read it) for how to build such a\n  struct inside `protected(...)`.\n* **W24** `png_set_check_for_invalid_index(png, allowed)` with allowed = -1, 0, 1 on palette\n  images: rows whose indices are all < num_palette (valid) AND rows with indices ≥ num_palette\n  (the C emits a specific warning/error on write — include it, but note that if it turns out to\n  be a fatal app error the trace still must match, which is the point; both libraries get the\n  same input). Log `png_get_palette_max` after each row.\n\nRULES:\n* Fixed seeds only (`Rng::new(<literal>)`); several inputs/shapes per configuration.\n* Never log a pointer/address — only null-ness, sizes and contents.\n* Keep `CString`/`Vec` backing storage alive OUTSIDE the `protected`/`with_write` closure.\n* Do NOT edit anything except your new `tests/write_b.rs`. Never touch `src/`, `c_src/`,\n  `tests/support/*`, `Cargo.toml`, or other test files (other agents are editing those).\n* If C and Rust genuinely diverge: KEEP the test, do NOT weaken it, do NOT `#[ignore]`, do NOT\n  modify `src/`. Report it precisely.\n* Run `timeout 600 cargo test --test write_b 2>&1 | tail -40`; iterate until it compiles and only\n  genuine divergences remain. Runtime under ~90 s.\n\nFINAL REPORT: per test fn — pass/fail, and for each failure the exact C-vs-Rust divergence plus\nthe configuration that triggered it."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2829,"cache_read_input_tokens":224727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2829,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"b2592df3-2ebf-4988-a046-fbed745a1bed","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:40:26.885Z"}
