{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KnVEQkr7W61KgTL53Gven1","type":"tool_result","content":"# CONFIGS.md — configuration surface (valid inputs) of the C implementation\n\nDerived from the branch structure of `c_src/src/*.c` and the public/internal API\nsurface (`png.h`: 218 `PNG_EXPORT` + 40 `PNG_FP/FIXED_EXPORT` entry points;\n`pngpriv.h`: 184 `PNG_INTERNAL_FUNCTION` entry points — **all** of them are\nexported from the `.so` and therefore all of them are directly callable).\n\nThe axes below are the ones the C code actually branches on:\n\n| axis | values the C distinguishes | where |\n|------|----------------------------|-------|\n| colour type | 0 GRAY, 2 RGB, 3 PALETTE, 4 GRAY_ALPHA, 6 RGB_ALPHA | `png_check_IHDR`, `png_read_start_row`, all row transforms |\n| bit depth | 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 (legal subset per colour type) | `png_check_IHDR`, `PNG_ROWBYTES`, sub-byte packing paths |\n| interlace | 0 none, 1 Adam7 (7 passes, per-pass geometry) | `png_do_read_interlace`, `png_do_write_interlace`, `png_combine_row` |\n| width/height | 1 (degenerate), small (sub-byte remainder), > 1 row buffer | `PNG_ROWBYTES` rounding, pass emptiness |\n| filter set | NONE / SUB / UP / AVG / PAETH / ALL, per-row heuristic | `png_write_find_filter`, `png_read_filter_row` |\n| zlib params | level 0/1/6/9, strategy, window bits 8..15, mem level 1..9, method | `png_write_IDAT`, `png_deflate_claim` |\n| IDAT buffering | `png_set_compression_buffer_size`, multi-IDAT split | `png_compress_IDAT` |\n| write API | `png_write_row` / `png_write_rows` / `png_write_image` / `png_write_png` | `pngwrite.c` |\n| read API | sequential (`png_read_row/rows/image/png`) / progressive (`png_process_data`) / simplified (`png_image_*`) | `pngread.c`, `pngpread.c` |\n| read transforms | the 26 `png_ptr->transformations` bits | `pngrtran.c` |\n| flush | `png_set_flush(n)` + `png_write_flush` | `png_write_row` |\n| ancillary chunks | every chunk in `PNG_KNOWN_CHUNKS` (24) + unknown chunks | `pngset.c`, `pngwutil.c`, `pngrutil.c` |\n| unknown handling | AS_DEFAULT / NEVER / IF_SAFE / ALWAYS, per-chunk list, user chunk callback | `png_handle_unknown` |\n| CRC action | DEFAULT / ERROR_QUIT / WARN_DISCARD / WARN_USE / QUIET_USE / NO_CHANGE, critical vs ancillary | `png_crc_finish`, `png_crc_error` |\n| limits | user width/height max, chunk cache max, chunk malloc max | `png_check_IHDR`, `png_handle_unknown` |\n| memory | default vs `png_create_*_struct_2` user malloc/free | `pngmem.c` |\n| number format | float (`png_set_gAMA`) vs fixed (`png_set_gAMA_fixed`) entry points | `pngset.c` |\n\nEach row below is exercised by a differential test that drives **both** `.so`s\nthrough the identical call sequence with pseudo-random (fixed-seed) data and\ncompares the complete trace — return values, every warning/error message, the\nproduced byte stream and every decoded row — byte for byte.\n\n## L — lowest-level entry points (called directly, no png_struct state)\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| L1 | `png_get_uint_32`, `png_get_uint_16`, `png_get_int_32` | 512 random 4-byte buffers + all boundary patterns (0, 0x7fffffff, 0x80000000, 0xffffffff) | [ ] |\n| L2 | `png_get_uint_31` | valid values < 2^31 (read struct present) | [ ] |\n| L3 | `png_save_uint_32`, `png_save_int_32`, `png_save_uint_16` | 512 random values incl. negative / boundary | [ ] |\n| L4 | `png_muldiv` | 512 random (a,times,div) triples: exact, rounding, negative, overflowing, div==0 | [ ] |\n| L5 | `png_reciprocal`, `png_reciprocal2` | random fixed-point values incl. 0 and extremes | [ ] |\n| L6 | `png_gamma_significant`, `png_gamma_correct`, `png_gamma_8bit_correct`, `png_gamma_16bit_correct` | random gamma × random sample, 8-bit and 16-bit | [ ] |\n| L7 | `png_XYZ_from_xy`, `png_xy_from_XYZ` | random chromaticities + sRGB values + degenerate (0 sums) | [ ] |\n| L8 | `png_check_fp_number`, `png_check_fp_string` | random ASCII, valid/invalid float syntax, embedded NUL, all state transitions | [ ] |\n| L9 | `png_ascii_from_fp`, `png_ascii_from_fixed` | random doubles/fixed × buffer sizes (exact fit, too small), precision 1..15 | [ ] |\n| L10 | `png_fixed`, `png_fixed_ITU` | random doubles in and out of the representable range | [ ] |\n| L11 | `png_check_keyword` | random keywords: leading/trailing/multiple spaces, control chars, >79 chars, empty | [ ] |\n| L12 | `png_safecat`, `png_format_number`, `png_warning_parameter*`, `png_formatted_warning` | random strings/positions, buffer overflow-by-one, all number formats | [ ] |\n| L13 | `png_build_grayscale_palette` | bit depth 1, 2, 4, 8 (+ invalid 3, 16 → nothing written) | [ ] |\n| L14 | `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer`, `png_convert_from_time_t`, `png_convert_from_struct_tm` | random png_time incl. out-of-range fields | [ ] |\n| L15 | `png_sig_cmp` | correct signature, every 1-byte corruption, all (start, num_to_check) pairs | [ ] |\n| L16 | `png_calculate_crc`, `png_reset_crc`, `png_crc_error` | random buffers over a read struct, critical/ancillary chunk names, all CRC actions | [ ] |\n| L17 | `png_sRGB_table`, `png_sRGB_base`, `png_sRGB_delta` (data symbols) | full table contents compared | [ ] |\n| L18 | `png_malloc`, `png_calloc`, `png_malloc_warn`, `png_malloc_base`, `png_malloc_array`, `png_realloc_array`, `png_free`, `png_zalloc`, `png_zfree` | sizes 0/1/small/huge, with and without user memory callbacks | [ ] |\n| L19 | `png_do_bgr`, `png_do_swap`, `png_do_invert`, `png_do_packswap`, `png_do_strip_channel`, `png_do_check_palette_indexes` | every colour type × bit depth × random row content | [ ] |\n| L20 | `png_read_filter_row` (+ `png_read_filter_row_*` via it) | filter 0..4 × pixel_depth 1..64 (bpp 1..8) × random rows/prev rows | [ ] |\n| L21 | `png_do_read_interlace`, `png_do_write_interlace` | pass 0..6 × bit depth 1..16 × colour type × random rows | [ ] |\n| L22 | `png_combine_row` | pass 0..6, display 0/1, bit depth 1..16, random dst/src | [ ] |\n| L23 | `png_access_version_number`, `png_get_copyright`, `png_get_header_ver`, `png_get_libpng_ver`, `png_get_header_version` | no state | [ ] |\n| L24 | `png_permit_mng_features`, `png_set_option` | every option index 0..11 × ON/OFF/unset, MNG feature mask bits | [ ] |\n| L25 | `png_icc_check_header`, `png_icc_check_length`, `png_icc_check_tag_table` | synthetic ICC profiles: valid minimal, every header field wrong | [ ] |\n| L26 | `png_build_gamma_table`, `png_destroy_gamma_table` | bit depth 8/16 × screen/file gamma combinations × 16-bit table shift | [ ] |\n| L27 | `png_info_init_3`, `png_create_info_struct`, `png_destroy_info_struct`, `png_data_freer`, `png_free_data` | every `PNG_FREE_*` mask × DESTROY/SET/USER freer | [ ] |\n| L28 | `png_check_IHDR` | every colour type × bit depth combination (legal and illegal) × width/height 0/1/max × interlace 0/1/2 | [ ] |\n| L29 | `png_zstream_error`, `png_reset_zstream`, `png_inflate_claim`, `png_zlib_inflate` | all zlib return codes reachable via crafted streams | [ ] |\n\n## W — write pipeline (`png_write_*`)\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| W1 | `png_write_row` | GRAY 1/2/4/8/16 bit, interlace none, width 1..17 (sub-byte remainders), random rows | [ ] |\n| W2 | `png_write_row` | RGB 8/16, interlace none | [ ] |\n| W3 | `png_write_row` | PALETTE 1/2/4/8 with random palette (+ tRNS), interlace none | [ ] |\n| W4 | `png_write_row` | GRAY_ALPHA 8/16, interlace none | [ ] |\n| W5 | `png_write_row` | RGB_ALPHA 8/16, interlace none | [ ] |\n| W6 | `png_write_row` | all 15 legal colour/depth combos, interlace **Adam7** (7 passes) | [ ] |\n| W7 | `png_write_rows` | all combos, num_rows 1 / all / more than remaining | [ ] |\n| W8 | `png_write_image` | all combos × interlace 0/1 (internal per-pass loop) | [ ] |\n=== W SECTION ===\n73:| W1 | `png_write_row` | GRAY 1/2/4/8/16 bit, interlace none, width 1..17 (sub-byte remainders), random rows | [ ] |\n74:| W2 | `png_write_row` | RGB 8/16, interlace none | [ ] |\n75:| W3 | `png_write_row` | PALETTE 1/2/4/8 with random palette (+ tRNS), interlace none | [ ] |\n76:| W4 | `png_write_row` | GRAY_ALPHA 8/16, interlace none | [ ] |\n77:| W5 | `png_write_row` | RGB_ALPHA 8/16, interlace none | [ ] |\n78:| W6 | `png_write_row` | all 15 legal colour/depth combos, interlace **Adam7** (7 passes) | [ ] |\n79:| W7 | `png_write_rows` | all combos, num_rows 1 / all / more than remaining | [ ] |\n80:| W8 | `png_write_image` | all combos × interlace 0/1 (internal per-pass loop) | [ ] |\n81:| W9 | `png_write_png` | every `PNG_TRANSFORM_*` write transform bit and combinations, via `png_set_rows` | [ ] |\n82:| W10 | `png_set_filter` | NONE / SUB / UP / AVG / PAETH / ALL / NO_FILTERS × colour type × depth (filter heuristic) | [ ] |\n83:| W11 | `png_set_compression_level` | 0, 1, 6, 9 × `png_set_compression_strategy` 0..4 | [ ] |\n84:| W12 | `png_set_compression_window_bits` | 8..15 (and the 8→9 clamp), × `png_set_compression_mem_level` 1..9 | [ ] |\n85:| W13 | `png_set_compression_method`, `png_set_compression_buffer_size` | method 8, buffer sizes 1, 2, 1024, huge (multi-IDAT split) | [ ] |\n86:| W14 | `png_set_flush` + `png_write_flush` | nrows 1, 2, 3, 0 (off) — flush callback ordering | [ ] |\n87:| W15 | `png_write_sig`, `png_write_chunk`, `png_write_chunk_start/data/end` | manual chunk emission, random names/payloads, zero-length | [ ] |\n88:| W16 | `png_write_info_before_PLTE` + `png_write_info` | split header write with palette/ancillary chunks | [ ] |\n89:| W17 | write transforms | `png_set_bgr`, `png_set_swap`, `png_set_packswap`, `png_set_invert_mono`, `png_set_invert_alpha`, `png_set_swap_alpha`, `png_set_filler(BEFORE/AFTER)`, `png_set_shift`, `png_set_packing` — each alone and all combinations that apply to the colour type | [ ] |\n90:| W18 | `png_set_write_user_transform_fn` + `png_set_user_transform_info` | user transform that rewrites the row, depth/channels overrides | [ ] |\n91:| W19 | `png_set_write_status_fn` | row/pass callback sequence for interlace 0/1 | [ ] |\n92:| W20 | `png_set_text` / `png_set_text_compression_*` | tEXt, zTXt (all compression levels/strategies/window bits/mem levels), iTXt (compressed + uncompressed, lang/lang_key) | [ ] |\n93:| W21 | `png_write_end` with an end-`info` | tIME + text after IDAT, and `png_write_end(NULL)` | [ ] |\n94:| W22 | 16-bit + `png_set_swap` + interlace + all filters | interaction of byte-swap with the filter heuristic | [ ] |\n95:| W23 | `png_create_write_struct_2` with user malloc/free | full write, allocation trace compared | [ ] |\n96:| W24 | `png_set_check_for_invalid_index` (write) | palette images with in-range and out-of-range indices | [ ] |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0142wgcwC4DU2gkmXGMTmwBC","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"9fe86758-f158-4d24-91ff-25523da24953","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:40:43.645Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write write_b tests W13-W24"}
