{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a4b316eba349d9208","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SAzHAkNEUsfGnGttcLZctZ","description":"Write read_b tests R17-R33","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration test file for a C→Rust differential verification of libpng 1.6.59.\n\nWorking dir: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust`\n\nFIRST read (short): `tests/HARNESS.md`, `tests/support/core.rs`, `tests/read_a.rs` (an existing\nexample of exactly this kind of file — copy its style and its input-building helpers), and the\n\"R\" section of `CONFIGS.md`. You implement rows **R17 through R33 only**.\n\nCREATE exactly one new file: `tests/read_b.rs`, one `#[test]` fn per row (`r17_...` … `r33_...`).\nEvery test drives BOTH `.so`s with `diff(...)` on IDENTICAL input bytes and compares the whole\ntrace byte-for-byte. Build inputs with `support::pngbuild` (independent of both libraries).\n\n* **R17** `png_set_shift(&PngColor8)`: inputs that carry an sBIT chunk (build the `sBIT` chunk\n  bytes yourself: 1 byte per channel for colour types 0/3, 3 for 2, 2 for 4, 4 for 6), 8-bit and\n  16-bit, random shift values in 1..bit_depth; also `png_set_shift` without any sBIT in the\n  stream.\n* **R18** `png_set_gamma` (double) and `png_set_gamma_fixed`: (screen_gamma, override_file_gamma)\n  pairs {(2.2,0.0), (1.0,1.0), (2.2,0.45455), (1.8,2.2), (0.0,0.0)} plus fixed-point extremes;\n  on inputs with and without a gAMA chunk, 8-bit and 16-bit, colour types 0/2/3/4/6. Read all\n  rows (the gamma tables are only observable through the transformed pixels).\n* **R19** `png_set_alpha_mode` / `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed`: mode PNG_ALPHA_PNG(0),\n  PNG_ALPHA_STANDARD(1), PNG_ALPHA_OPTIMIZED(2), PNG_ALPHA_BROKEN(3) × output gamma\n  {1.0, 2.2, 0.45455, sRGB fixed 45455/220000} × inputs with alpha (4/6) and without (0/2/3),\n  8-bit and 16-bit.\n* **R20** `png_set_background` / `png_set_background_fixed`: background_gamma_code\n  PNG_BACKGROUND_GAMMA_UNKNOWN/SCREEN/FILE/UNIQUE (0..3) × need_expand 0/1 × background colour\n  (`PngColor16`: palette index for colour type 3, grey, RGB, 16-bit values) × inputs with tRNS\n  and with an alpha channel, 8-bit and 16-bit. Combine with `png_set_gamma` in half the cases\n  (that is the composite path in `pngrtran.c`).\n* **R21** `png_set_quantize(png, palette, num_palette, maximum_colors, histogram, full_quantize)`:\n  full_quantize 0 and 1 × maximum_colors 2, 4, 16, 100, 256 × with a NULL histogram and with a\n  random `u16` histogram × palette input (pass the image's own palette) and RGB/RGBA input\n  (pass a random palette). Log the returned palette contents afterwards\n  (`png_get_PLTE`) and all rows.\n* **R22** `png_set_read_user_transform_fn` + `png_set_user_transform_info`: an\n  `unsafe extern \"C\" fn(Png, *mut PngRowInfo, *mut u8)` callback that logs the `PngRowInfo`\n  fields and the row bytes and then rewrites the row deterministically; combined with\n  `png_set_expand`/`png_set_gray_to_rgb` in some cases; log `png_get_user_transform_ptr`\n  null-ness. Also set `user_transform_depth`/`channels` and check `png_get_rowbytes`.\n* **R23** `png_set_read_status_fn`: callback `unsafe extern \"C\" fn(Png, u32, c_int)` logging\n  (row, pass); interlace 0 and 1; via `png_read_row`, `png_read_rows` and `png_read_image`.\n* **R24** `png_set_crc_action(png, crit_action, ancil_action)`: all 6 × 6 combinations\n  (PNG_CRC_DEFAULT..PNG_CRC_NO_CHANGE = 0..5) on three inputs: all CRCs correct; an ancillary\n  chunk with a bad CRC (`pngbuild::Chunk::new(b\"tEXt\", ...).bad_crc()`); a critical chunk (IDAT\n  and, separately, IHDR/PLTE) with a bad CRC. Each combination is its own `diff` run so a fatal\n  error in one does not hide the others.\n* **R25** `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks(png, keep, chunk_list, num_chunks)` with keep =\n  PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT/NEVER/IF_SAFE/ALWAYS (0..3) and also keep = -1 (the documented\n  \"default\" reset) × chunk_list NULL / a list of 1..3 names × input containing several unknown\n  chunks (private names, some with the \"safe to copy\" bit set and some without, before PLTE,\n  before IDAT and after IDAT). Plus `png_set_read_user_chunk_fn(png, user_ptr, cb)` with a\n  callback returning -1, 0 and 1 (log the chunk name/size it receives), and\n  `png_get_user_chunk_ptr` null-ness, and `png_handle_as_unknown` for every chunk name.\n* **R26** `png_set_user_limits(png, w, h)`, `png_set_chunk_cache_max(png, n)`,\n  `png_set_chunk_malloc_max(png, n)`: limits ABOVE the actual image/chunk sizes (the valid\n  path — the rejecting cases are Phase C rows, but include them too since the messages must\n  match: use a separate `diff` run per limit so an error does not hide later checks). Log\n  `png_get_user_width_max`, `png_get_user_height_max`, `png_get_chunk_cache_max`,\n  `png_get_chunk_malloc_max`.\n* **R27** `png_set_sig_bytes(png, n)` for n = 0..8: feed the stream with the first n signature\n  bytes already removed, which is the documented usage.\n* **R28** `png_start_read_image` and `png_read_update_info`: the documented sequences —\n  `read_info` → `read_update_info` → rows; `read_info` → `start_read_image` → rows;\n  `read_info` → `read_update_info` → `read_update_info` (the C warns on the second call — keep\n  the warning); `read_info` → rows without either call; with transforms set in each case.\n* **R29** `png_read_end(png, end_info)` with a second info struct, and with NULL; inputs with\n  ancillary chunks after IDAT (tEXt, tIME, unknown) and with data after IEND; log everything\n  from the end-info struct with `log_all_info`.\n* **R30** transform stacking: for every colour type/bit depth, apply the whole pipeline\n  `png_set_expand` + `png_set_gray_to_rgb` + `png_set_add_alpha(0xffff, AFTER)` +\n  `png_set_swap` + `png_set_bgr` + `png_set_strip_16` (and a second variant with\n  `png_set_scale_16` and `png_set_swap_alpha`), plus 8 seeded random subsets of that set. Read\n  every row and log `png_get_rowbytes`/`png_get_channels` after `png_read_update_info`.\n* **R31** `png_create_read_struct_2` with the harness `cb_malloc`/`cb_free` and\n  `with_session(|s| s.trace_alloc = true)`: full read of several images so every allocation size\n  and order is compared. Turn `trace_alloc` ON only after `png_create_read_struct_2` +\n  `png_set_longjmp_fn` (the size of `png_struct` itself legitimately differs). See\n  `tests/lowlevel_a.rs` fn `l18_memory` for the pattern.\n* **R32** `png_get_io_state` and `png_get_io_chunk_type`: poll them from inside the read\n  callback. The harness `cb_read` cannot see the png_ptr conveniently, so instead install your\n  own read callback in this test that logs `png_get_io_state`/`png_get_io_chunk_type` — you can\n  get the `Core` for the current library into the callback via a `thread_local` set before the\n  run (a raw pointer to a small struct holding the two function pointers). Log the\n  state/chunk-type sequence for a full read.\n* **R33** `png_get_current_row_number` / `png_get_current_pass_number`: poll after every\n  `png_read_row` for interlace 0 and 1, several colour types.\n\nRULES:\n* Fixed seeds only (`Rng::new(<literal>)`); several inputs per configuration.\n* Never log a pointer/address — only null-ness, sizes, contents.\n* Do NOT edit anything except your new `tests/read_b.rs`. Never touch `src/`, `c_src/`,\n  `tests/support/*`, `Cargo.toml`, or other test files (other agents are editing those).\n* If C and Rust genuinely diverge: KEEP the test, do NOT weaken it, do NOT `#[ignore]`, do NOT\n  modify `src/`. Report it precisely (row, configuration, the two trace lines).\n* Run `timeout 600 cargo test --test read_b 2>&1 | tail -40`; iterate until it compiles and only\n  genuine divergences remain. Runtime under ~90 s (images ≤ 17×8).\n\nFINAL REPORT: per test fn — pass/fail, and for each failure the exact C-vs-Rust trace difference\nplus the triggering configuration.","uuid":"246f0a65-041d-4091-9b27-ba1e6fffc034","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e"}
