{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6f2p33au5zufmimgh2apjv6h5kqj3ply7ts6eav3nrwoocngsxvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Final state verified. Here is the report.\n\n## What was created\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust/tests/read_a.rs` (only file touched; nothing else modified) — 16 `#[test]` fns `r1_…`–`r16_…`, ~5 000 differential configurations (~10 000 read cycles), **2.2 s** total runtime.\n\nEvery case builds its PNG with `support::pngbuild` (PLTE sized `1<<bit_depth` so all indices are in range; optional tRNS/sBIT/gAMA in canonical chunk order; a hand-built raw stream with row filters cycling 0..4; a hand-built all-grey RGB/RGBA stream for R12) and drives both `.so`s through `diff(...)` + `with_read(...)` on identical bytes. Row buffers are zero-filled once per case, `rowbytes` bytes are logged plus 16 separate slack bytes; interlaced input uses `png_set_interlace_handling` + `height` rows per pass (7 passes), as libpng requires.\n\n## Results\n\n| test | result |\n|---|---|\n| r1_read_row_all_combos (15 combos × il 0/1 × w 1,3,7,8,17 × h 1,5 × 2 seeds × filter-0/all-5-filters) | **pass** |\n| r2_read_rows (num_rows 1/all × row-only/display-only/both) | **pass** |\n| r3_read_image (incl. the \"Interlace handling should be turned on\" warning path) | **pass** |\n| r4_read_png_transforms | **FAIL** (SWAP_ALPHA only) |\n| r5_interlace_handling (all 7 passes, + `get_current_pass/row_number` per row) | **pass** |\n| r6_packing, r7_packswap (+packing, both orders, + no-op depths) | **pass** |\n| r8_expand, r9_expand_16, r10_expand_parts (matching + non-matching colour types) | **pass** |\n| r11_gray_to_rgb | **pass** |\n| r12_rgb_to_gray (fp + fixed × action 1/2/3 × 5 coeff pairs × grey/non-grey rows, status logged per row) | **pass** |\n| r13_strip_scale_16, r14_strip_alpha, r15_filler_add_alpha | **pass** |\n| r16_byte_order_transforms | **FAIL** (swap_alpha on RGBA-16 only) |\n\n## The one genuine divergence (2 failing tests, 46 failing configurations)\n\n`png_do_read_swap_alpha`, **RGB_ALPHA 16-bit branch**, `src/pngrtran.rs:1962-1989`: it performs only **4** `*dp = *sp` byte copies where C (`c_src/src/pngrtran.c:2646-2663`) performs **6**. So the alpha is deposited at byte offset 2 instead of 0 and both cursors advance 6 bytes per pixel instead of 8, shredding the whole row. The GRAY_ALPHA-16 and both 8-bit branches are correct.\n\nR16, `png_set_swap_alpha`, RGBA 16-bit, w=1, h=3, il=0, seed 0x16000+…: input pixel `9569 3fae 63ef 8af6` (r,g,b,a)\n```\nC   : p0r0=8af695693fae63ef slack=00000000000000000000000000000000   (a,r,g,b - correct ARGB)\nRUST: p0r0=95698af63fae63ef slack=00000000000000000000000000000000   (r,a,g,b)\n```\nR4, `png_read_png(PNG_TRANSFORM_SWAP_ALPHA)`, RGBA 16-bit, w=8, h=3, il=0:\n```\nC   : row0=a201257940dc654ed02fe573e46fd55af2a05e81e08cb971403b4039b15077911ecb78b2ae9612c41308d6e8d7ad605aa3e06721c1944cb1423eaa404498837a\nRUST: row0=257940dc654ea201e573e46fd55ad02fb9715e81e08cb150f2a0403978b27791403b1ecbae9612c4605ad6e8d7adc19413086721aa404cb1a3e0423e4498837a\n```\nFull failing set (enumerated with a temporary catch_unwind build, not part of the committed file): R16 `swap_alpha`, `invert_alpha+swap_alpha`, `swap+swap_alpha`, `bgr+swap_alpha`, `swap+bgr+invert_alpha+swap_alpha` — each at ct=6/bd=16 × w 1,7 × il 0,1 × 2 seeds (40 cases); R4 `tr=SWAP_ALPHA` ct=6 bd=16 (w 8 and 5) and `rand0=0x0114` (SWAP_ALPHA|EXPAND|PACKING) at ct=2 and ct=6, bd=16, il=1 — the ct=2 case reaches RGBA-16 via EXPAND of tRNS (6 cases). With those excluded, all 16 tests pass, i.e. this is the only divergence in R1–R16. Tests were left intact, not ignored, and `src/` was not touched.\n\n## Two harness facts worth knowing (both handled inside my file)\n\n1. `target/cbuild/libpng.so` is linked **without `-lm`** (`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` links only ZLIB), so the first float entry point called in the C reference kills the test process with `symbol lookup error: undefined symbol: floor` (hit by `png_set_rgb_to_gray` → `png_fixed` → `floor`; `pow` is also unresolved). `ensure_libm()` in `tests/read_a.rs` dlopens `libm.so.6` with `RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL` before any test runs. Any other test file touching the float API (`png_set_gamma`, gamma tables, `png_set_background`, sCAL/gAMA float getters) will need the same, or the C `.so` should be linked with `m`.\n2. `png_read_png` allocates its row buffers with `png_malloc` (uninitialised) and `png_combine_row` deliberately **preserves** the last byte's bits beyond the image width, so for sub-byte widths those padding bits are uninitialised heap in *both* libraries (this produced a spurious `row1=97` vs `93` on GRAY-1 w=5). R4 therefore masks the last byte with the width/PACKSWAP-derived mask (the mask is logged) and additionally runs every case at w=8 where nothing is masked. Padding-bit preservation itself is still verified deterministically by R1/R5/R6/R7, which read into caller buffers this file zero-fills first."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1467,"cache_read_input_tokens":245367,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1467,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BT74adzj7YMyi2Z4qaNgxx","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"cc5a1ee5-5bcb-4a63-a17d-4ab2a8cf05e5","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:41:39.417Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write read transform tests R1-R16"}
