{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WLEBz72EL94HD5GqZaGfqD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md — configuration surface (valid inputs) of the C implementation\n2\t\n3\tDerived from the branch structure of `c_src/src/*.c` and the public/internal API\n4\tsurface (`png.h`: 218 `PNG_EXPORT` + 40 `PNG_FP/FIXED_EXPORT` entry points;\n5\t`pngpriv.h`: 184 `PNG_INTERNAL_FUNCTION` entry points — **all** of them are\n6\texported from the `.so` and therefore all of them are directly callable).\n7\t\n8\tThe axes below are the ones the C code actually branches on:\n9\t\n10\t| axis | values the C distinguishes | where |\n11\t|------|----------------------------|-------|\n12\t| colour type | 0 GRAY, 2 RGB, 3 PALETTE, 4 GRAY_ALPHA, 6 RGB_ALPHA | `png_check_IHDR`, `png_read_start_row`, all row transforms |\n13\t| bit depth | 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 (legal subset per colour type) | `png_check_IHDR`, `PNG_ROWBYTES`, sub-byte packing paths |\n14\t| interlace | 0 none, 1 Adam7 (7 passes, per-pass geometry) | `png_do_read_interlace`, `png_do_write_interlace`, `png_combine_row` |\n15\t| width/height | 1 (degenerate), small (sub-byte remainder), > 1 row buffer | `PNG_ROWBYTES` rounding, pass emptiness |\n16\t| filter set | NONE / SUB / UP / AVG / PAETH / ALL, per-row heuristic | `png_write_find_filter`, `png_read_filter_row` |\n17\t| zlib params | level 0/1/6/9, strategy, window bits 8..15, mem level 1..9, method | `png_write_IDAT`, `png_deflate_claim` |\n18\t| IDAT buffering | `png_set_compression_buffer_size`, multi-IDAT split | `png_compress_IDAT` |\n19\t| write API | `png_write_row` / `png_write_rows` / `png_write_image` / `png_write_png` | `pngwrite.c` |\n20\t| read API | sequential (`png_read_row/rows/image/png`) / progressive (`png_process_data`) / simplified (`png_image_*`) | `pngread.c`, `pngpread.c` |\n21\t| read transforms | the 26 `png_ptr->transformations` bits | `pngrtran.c` |\n22\t| flush | `png_set_flush(n)` + `png_write_flush` | `png_write_row` |\n23\t| ancillary chunks | every chunk in `PNG_KNOWN_CHUNKS` (24) + unknown chunks | `pngset.c`, `pngwutil.c`, `pngrutil.c` |\n24\t| unknown handling | AS_DEFAULT / NEVER / IF_SAFE / ALWAYS, per-chunk list, user chunk callback | `png_handle_unknown` |\n25\t| CRC action | DEFAULT / ERROR_QUIT / WARN_DISCARD / WARN_USE / QUIET_USE / NO_CHANGE, critical vs ancillary | `png_crc_finish`, `png_crc_error` |\n26\t| limits | user width/height max, chunk cache max, chunk malloc max | `png_check_IHDR`, `png_handle_unknown` |\n27\t| memory | default vs `png_create_*_struct_2` user malloc/free | `pngmem.c` |\n28\t| number format | float (`png_set_gAMA`) vs fixed (`png_set_gAMA_fixed`) entry points | `pngset.c` |\n29\t\n30\tEach row below is exercised by a differential test that drives **both** `.so`s\n31\tthrough the identical call sequence with pseudo-random (fixed-seed) data and\n32\tcompares the complete trace — return values, every warning/error message, the\n33\tproduced byte stream and every decoded row — byte for byte.\n34\t\n35\t## L — lowest-level entry points (called directly, no png_struct state)\n36\t\n37\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n38\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n39\t| L1 | `png_get_uint_32`, `png_get_uint_16`, `png_get_int_32` | 512 random 4-byte buffers + all boundary patterns (0, 0x7fffffff, 0x80000000, 0xffffffff) | [x] |\n40\t| L2 | `png_get_uint_31` | valid values < 2^31 (read struct present) | [x] |\n41\t| L3 | `png_save_uint_32`, `png_save_int_32`, `png_save_uint_16` | 512 random values incl. negative / boundary | [x] |\n42\t| L4 | `png_muldiv` | 512 random (a,times,div) triples: exact, rounding, negative, overflowing, div==0 | [x] |\n43\t| L5 | `png_reciprocal`, `png_reciprocal2` | random fixed-point values incl. 0 and extremes | [x] |\n44\t| L6 | `png_gamma_significant`, `png_gamma_correct`, `png_gamma_8bit_correct`, `png_gamma_16bit_correct` | random gamma × random sample, 8-bit and 16-bit | [x] |\n45\t| L7 | `png_XYZ_from_xy`, `png_xy_from_XYZ` | random chromaticities + sRGB values + degenerate (0 sums) | [x] |\n46\t| L8 | `png_check_fp_number`, `png_check_fp_string` | random ASCII, valid/invalid float syntax, embedded NUL, all state transitions | [x] |\n47\t| L9 | `png_ascii_from_fp`, `png_ascii_from_fixed` | random doubles/fixed × buffer sizes (exact fit, too small), precision 1..15 | [x] |\n48\t| L10 | `png_fixed`, `png_fixed_ITU` | random doubles in and out of the representable range | [x] |\n49\t| L11 | `png_check_keyword` | random keywords: leading/trailing/multiple spaces, control chars, >79 chars, empty | [x] |\n50\t| L12 | `png_safecat`, `png_format_number`, `png_warning_parameter*`, `png_formatted_warning` | random strings/positions, buffer overflow-by-one, all number formats | [x] |\n51\t| L13 | `png_build_grayscale_palette` | bit depth 1, 2, 4, 8 (+ invalid 3, 16 → nothing written) | [x] |\n52\t| L14 | `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer`, `png_convert_from_time_t`, `png_convert_from_struct_tm` | random png_time incl. out-of-range fields | [x] |\n53\t| L15 | `png_sig_cmp` | correct signature, every 1-byte corruption, all (start, num_to_check) pairs | [x] |\n54\t| L16 | `png_calculate_crc`, `png_reset_crc`, `png_crc_error` | random buffers over a read struct, critical/ancillary chunk names, all CRC actions | [x] |\n55\t| L17 | `png_sRGB_table`, `png_sRGB_base`, `png_sRGB_delta` (data symbols) | full table contents compared | [x] |\n56\t| L18 | `png_malloc`, `png_calloc`, `png_malloc_warn`, `png_malloc_base`, `png_malloc_array`, `png_realloc_array`, `png_free`, `png_zalloc`, `png_zfree` | sizes 0/1/small/huge, with and without user memory callbacks | [x] |\n57\t| L19 | `png_do_bgr`, `png_do_swap`, `png_do_invert`, `png_do_packswap`, `png_do_strip_channel`, `png_do_check_palette_indexes` | every colour type × bit depth × random row content | [x] |\n58\t| L20 | `png_read_filter_row` (+ `png_read_filter_row_*` via it) | filter 0..4 × pixel_depth 1..64 (bpp 1..8) × random rows/prev rows | [x] |\n59\t| L21 | `png_do_read_interlace`, `png_do_write_interlace` | pass 0..6 × bit depth 1..16 × colour type × random rows | [x] |\n60\t| L22 | `png_combine_row` | pass 0..6, display 0/1, bit depth 1..16, random dst/src | [x] |\n61\t| L23 | `png_access_version_number`, `png_get_copyright`, `png_get_header_ver`, `png_get_libpng_ver`, `png_get_header_version` | no state | [x] |\n62\t| L24 | `png_permit_mng_features`, `png_set_option` | every option index 0..11 × ON/OFF/unset, MNG feature mask bits | [x] |\n63\t| L25 | `png_icc_check_header`, `png_icc_check_length`, `png_icc_check_tag_table` | synthetic ICC profiles: valid minimal, every header field wrong | [x] |\n64\t| L26 | `png_build_gamma_table`, `png_destroy_gamma_table` | bit depth 8/16 × screen/file gamma combinations × 16-bit table shift | [x] |\n65\t| L27 | `png_info_init_3`, `png_create_info_struct`, `png_destroy_info_struct`, `png_data_freer`, `png_free_data` | every `PNG_FREE_*` mask × DESTROY/SET/USER freer | [x] |\n66\t| L28 | `png_check_IHDR` | every colour type × bit depth combination (legal and illegal) × width/height 0/1/max × interlace 0/1/2 | [x] |\n67\t| L29 | `png_zstream_error`, `png_reset_zstream`, `png_inflate_claim`, `png_zlib_inflate` | all zlib return codes reachable via crafted streams | [x] |\n68\t\n69\t## W — write pipeline (`png_write_*`)\n70\t\n71\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n72\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n73\t| W1 | `png_write_row` | GRAY 1/2/4/8/16 bit, interlace none, width 1..17 (sub-byte remainders), random rows | [x] |\n74\t| W2 | `png_write_row` | RGB 8/16, interlace none | [x] |\n75\t| W3 | `png_write_row` | PALETTE 1/2/4/8 with random palette (+ tRNS), interlace none | [x] |\n76\t| W4 | `png_write_row` | GRAY_ALPHA 8/16, interlace none | [x] |\n77\t| W5 | `png_write_row` | RGB_ALPHA 8/16, interlace none | [x] |\n78\t| W6 | `png_write_row` | all 15 legal colour/depth combos, interlace **Adam7** (7 passes) | [x] |\n79\t| W7 | `png_write_rows` | all combos, num_rows 1 / all / more than remaining | [x] |\n80\t| W8 | `png_write_image` | all combos × interlace 0/1 (internal per-pass loop) | [x] |\n81\t| W9 | `png_write_png` | every `PNG_TRANSFORM_*` write transform bit and combinations, via `png_set_rows` | [x] |\n82\t| W10 | `png_set_filter` | NONE / SUB / UP / AVG / PAETH / ALL / NO_FILTERS × colour type × depth (filter heuristic) | [x] |\n83\t| W11 | `png_set_compression_level` | 0, 1, 6, 9 × `png_set_compression_strategy` 0..4 | [x] |\n84\t| W12 | `png_set_compression_window_bits` | 8..15 (and the 8→9 clamp), × `png_set_compression_mem_level` 1..9 | [x] |\n85\t| W13 | `png_set_compression_method`, `png_set_compression_buffer_size` | method 8, buffer sizes 1, 2, 1024, huge (multi-IDAT split) | [ ] |\n86\t| W14 | `png_set_flush` + `png_write_flush` | nrows 1, 2, 3, 0 (off) — flush callback ordering | [ ] |\n87\t| W15 | `png_write_sig`, `png_write_chunk`, `png_write_chunk_start/data/end` | manual chunk emission, random names/payloads, zero-length | [ ] |\n88\t| W16 | `png_write_info_before_PLTE` + `png_write_info` | split header write with palette/ancillary chunks | [ ] |\n89\t| W17 | write transforms | `png_set_bgr`, `png_set_swap`, `png_set_packswap`, `png_set_invert_mono`, `png_set_invert_alpha`, `png_set_swap_alpha`, `png_set_filler(BEFORE/AFTER)`, `png_set_shift`, `png_set_packing` — each alone and all combinations that apply to the colour type | [ ] |\n90\t| W18 | `png_set_write_user_transform_fn` + `png_set_user_transform_info` | user transform that rewrites the row, depth/channels overrides | [ ] |\n91\t| W19 | `png_set_write_status_fn` | row/pass callback sequence for interlace 0/1 | [ ] |\n92\t| W20 | `png_set_text` / `png_set_text_compression_*` | tEXt, zTXt (all compression levels/strategies/window bits/mem levels), iTXt (compressed + uncompressed, lang/lang_key) | [ ] |\n93\t| W21 | `png_write_end` with an end-`info` | tIME + text after IDAT, and `png_write_end(NULL)` | [ ] |\n94\t| W22 | 16-bit + `png_set_swap` + interlace + all filters | interaction of byte-swap with the filter heuristic | [ ] |\n95\t| W23 | `png_create_write_struct_2` with user malloc/free | full write, allocation trace compared | [ ] |\n96\t| W24 | `png_set_check_for_invalid_index` (write) | palette images with in-range and out-of-range indices | [ ] |\n97\t\n98\t## C — chunk set/get round trips (`pngset.c` ↔ `pngget.c` ↔ `pngwutil.c` ↔ `pngrutil.c`)\n99\t\n100\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n101\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n102\t| C1 | `png_set_PLTE`/`png_get_PLTE` | 1, 2, 16, 255, 256 entries × bit depth; palette on RGB image | [ ] |\n103\t| C2 | `png_set_tRNS`/`png_get_tRNS` | palette alpha (1..256 entries), grey key, RGB key, 16-bit values | [ ] |\n104\t| C3 | `png_set_gAMA`/`_fixed` + getters | random gammas incl. 0, 1, 100000, > limits, float and fixed entry points | [ ] |\n105\t| C4 | `png_set_sRGB`, `png_set_sRGB_gAMA_and_cHRM` | intent 0..3 | [ ] |\n106\t| C5 | `png_set_cHRM`/`_fixed`/`_XYZ`/`_XYZ_fixed` + getters | random valid chromaticities, sRGB endpoints, XYZ round trip | [ ] |\n107\t| C6 | `png_set_iCCP`/`png_get_iCCP` | synthetic profiles 132..4096 bytes, keyword lengths 1..79, compressed round trip | [ ] |\n108\t| C7 | `png_set_sBIT`/getter | every colour type with legal sBIT values (and the maxima) | [ ] |\n109\t| C8 | `png_set_bKGD`/getter | palette index, grey, RGB, 16-bit | [ ] |\n110\t| C9 | `png_set_hIST`/getter | palette sizes 1..256, random frequencies | [ ] |\n111\t| C10 | `png_set_pHYs`/getters (`png_get_pHYs_dpi`, `png_get_x_pixels_per_*`, aspect ratio) | random resolutions × unit 0/1 | [ ] |\n112\t| C11 | `png_set_oFFs`/getters (`png_get_x_offset_*`) | negative/positive offsets × unit 0/1 | [ ] |\n113\t| C12 | `png_set_tIME`/getter + `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` | random times incl. field extremes | [ ] |\n114\t| C13 | `png_set_pCAL`/getter | equation type 0..3 × nparams 0..3 × random ASCII params | [ ] |\n115\t| C14 | `png_set_sCAL`/`_fixed`/`_s` + getters | unit 1/2 × random dimensions (float, fixed, string forms) | [ ] |\n116\t| C15 | `png_set_sPLT`/getter | 1..3 palettes × depth 8/16 × 1..16 entries, names with spaces | [ ] |\n117\t| C16 | `png_set_eXIf_1`/getter | random EXIF blobs (II/MM headers), lengths 4..1024 | [ ] |\n118\t| C17 | `png_set_cICP`/getter | random primaries/transfer/matrix/full-range | [ ] |\n119\t| C18 | `png_set_cLLI`/`_fixed`/getter | random maxCLL/maxFALL incl. 0 | [ ] |\n120\t| C19 | `png_set_mDCV`/`_fixed`/getter | random display primaries/white point/luminances | [ ] |\n121\t| C20 | `png_set_text`/`png_get_text` | tEXt/zTXt/iTXt mixes, 1..8 entries, empty text, 8-bit chars, NULL text | [ ] |\n122\t| C21 | `png_set_unknown_chunks` + `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` + `png_get_unknown_chunks` | before-PLTE / before-IDAT / after-IDAT locations, 0-length data, critical-looking names | [ ] |\n123\t| C22 | `png_set_rows`/`png_get_rows` + `png_free_data(PNG_FREE_ROWS)` | round trip through `png_write_png`/`png_read_png` | [ ] |\n124\t| C23 | `png_set_invalid`, `png_get_valid` | every `PNG_INFO_*` flag | [ ] |\n125\t| C24 | full-chunk PNG | ONE image carrying **every** supported ancillary chunk, written then read, all getters compared | [ ] |\n126\t\n127\t## R — sequential read pipeline (`pngread.c`, `pngrutil.c`, `pngrtran.c`)\n128\t\n129\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n130\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n131\t| R1 | `png_read_info` + `png_read_row` | all 15 colour/depth combos × interlace 0/1, no transforms | [x] |\n132\t| R2 | `png_read_rows` | num_rows 1 / all, with and without `display_row` | [x] |\n133\t| R3 | `png_read_image` | all combos × interlace 0/1 (internal