ll 9 IDAT zlib variants yield distinct messages (`invalid window size (libpng)`, `unknown compression method`, `incorrect header check`, `invalid stored block lengths`, `incorrect data check`, `missing LZ dictionary`, `Not enough image data`), and all 12 `png_zstream_error` texts appear.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Build gap in the C reference `.so` (not a translation bug, but it blocks any float path).** `target/cbuild/libpng.so` has `NEEDED` only for `libz.so.1`/`libc.so.6` — `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` never links libm. On glibc 2.34 `floor`/`pow`/`frexp`/`modf` still live in `libm.so.6`, and because the harness `dlopen`s both libraries with `RTLD_LOCAL`, the C library can only resolve them from the executable's global scope. The first gamma test aborted the whole binary with `symbol lookup error: target/cbuild/libpng.so: undefined symbol: floor`. Fixed **inside my test file** (`#[link(name = \"m\")]` + `l00_libm_is_linked`, which keeps `libm.so.6` in the test binary's `DT_NEEDED` under `--as-needed`). **Any other test group that reaches gamma / `png_ascii_from_fp` / fixed-point float code in the C lib will hit the same wall** — the durable fix would be `-DCMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS=-lm` when configuring `target/cbuild`, or `target_link_libraries(png PRIVATE m)` in `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` (I did not touch either).\n\n2. **No C↔Rust divergence.** Nothing was weakened, ignored, or removed; `src/`, `c_src/`, `tests/support/*`, `Cargo.toml` and other test files are untouched.\n\n3. Two issues I hit were bugs in my own driver, both fixed properly rather than by relaxing anything:\n   - `png_free_data(PNG_FREE_TEXT, num != -1)` frees only `text[num].key`, but `png_set_text_2` allocates `key`/`text`/`lang`/`lang_key` as **one** block — so `text[num].text` is left dangling by libpng. Logging its contents was reading freed heap (which legitimately differs between processes). Those entries are now logged structurally (null-ness, lengths, compression) via `log_info_state_notext`.\n   - The progressive reader requires the *info* callback to call `png_read_update_info()`/`png_start_read_image()`; without it `row_buf` is never set up and every image degenerated to `WARNING(Truncated compressed data in IDAT)` with zero row callbacks. `prog_info` now calls it, and `png_progressive_combine_row` is genuinely exercised across all 7 passes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1417,"cache_read_input_tokens":346500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1417,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KKgwxwravRomJENipvomj6","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"902c21b8-86e1-4145-ac0b-bccedb981034","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:46:38.388Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lowlevel_b tests L19-L29"}
