{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01YayHobMcc7tsyDEJrwGj42","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ERRORS.md — error / rejection surface of the C implementation\n2\t\n3\tDerived **mechanically** from `c_src/src/*.c` (`tmp/gen_errors.py`): every call to an\n4\terror/warning/report macro, every sentinel `return 0 / NULL / -1` in an *exported*\n5\tfunction, and every `assert`.  One row per distinct rejection site.\n6\t\n7\tSemantics of the \"expected C result\" column (see `pngerror.c`, `pnglibconf.h` —\n8\tthis build has `PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` + `PNG_BENIGN_READ_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`\n9\tbut **not** `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`, and `PNG_ERROR_NUMBERS` is off):\n10\t\n11\t* `png_error` / `png_chunk_error` / `png_fixed_error` — call `error_fn` with the exact\n12\t  message, then `longjmp` (harness returns non-zero `rc`).\n13\t* `png_app_error` — fatal unless `PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN` (set by\n14\t  `png_set_benign_errors(1)`), else a warning.\n15\t* `png_benign_error` / `png_chunk_benign_error` — on a **read** struct: warning when\n16\t  `PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN` is set, otherwise fatal; on a **write** struct always fatal.\n17\t* `png_warning` / `png_app_warning` / `png_chunk_warning` — `warning_fn` with the exact\n18\t  message, execution continues.\n19\t* `png_chunk_report(..., PNG_CHUNK_ERROR|WARNING|WRITE_ERROR)` — dispatches to the above.\n20\t* `png_image_error` — simplified API: stores the message in `image->message`, returns 0.\n21\t* `png_zstream_error` — records a zlib message consumed by a later error/warning.\n22\t\n23\tEvery row is exercised by the Phase C differential tests: both libraries are driven\n24\tinto the condition and the *complete* message/return trace must be byte identical.\n25\tCoverage is verified mechanically by `tests/error_coverage.rs`, which records every\n26\tmessage string emitted by the C library and requires the Rust library to emit the\n27\tidentical sequence (see `ERROR_COVE