13 offsets incl. `i32::MIN`/`MAX` × unit 0/1/2, all 8 derived getters incl. `_fixed` |\n| `c12_time` | C12 | pass | 14 times (field extremes, 3 rejected-by-setter cases, 7 random) + `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` on the value read back |\n| `c13_pcal` | C13 | pass | type 0..3 × nparams 0..3 (+ the legal (3,4)), random fp param strings, 8-bit purpose/units |\n| `c14_scal` | C14 | pass | unit 1/2 × 4 double + 4 fixed + 5 string forms; `png_get_sCAL`, `_fixed`, `_s` all logged |\n| `c15_splt` | C15 | pass | 1..3 palettes × depth 8/16 × 3 seeds, 1..16 entries, names with internal spaces |\n| `c16_exif` | C16 | pass | II/MM BOM × lengths 4/5/8/33/128/1024 + the deprecated `png_set_eXIf`/`png_get_eXIf` |\n| `c17_cicp` | C17 | pass | 12 (primaries, transfer, matrix, range) incl. matrix≠0 rejection |\n| `c18_clli` | C18 | pass | 12 fixed (incl. 0 and 0x7FFFFFFF) + 8 double, both getters |\n| `c19_mdcv` | C19 | pass | 10 fixed (incl. odd values that lose the low bit in the /2 encoding) + 7 double, both getters |\n| `c20_text` | C20 | pass | 1..8 entries × 3 seeds mixing tEXt/zTXt/iTXt-none/iTXt-zTXt, empty text, 8-bit text, NULL `text`, NULL `lang`/`lang_key`, plus two consecutive `png_set_text` calls |\n| `c21_unknown` | C21 | pass | 1..4 chunks (`prVt`/`teSt`/`abCd`/`xyZw`, one always 0-length) × 3 relocations × 2 seeds, `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks(ALWAYS)` + `png_handle_as_unknown` on read |\n| `c22_rows_png` | C22 | pass | all 15 colour/depth combos × widths 1/8/9 through `png_set_rows`+`png_write_png`/`png_read_png`+`png_free_data(PNG_FREE_ROWS,-1)` |\n| `c23_set_invalid` | C23 | pass | every-chunk image + baseline + each of the 20 `PNG_INFO_*` flags invalidated individually + 5 combined masks |\n| `c24_everything` | C24 | pass | every ancillary chunk at once on palette-8 and RGBA-16 (and grey-16), each with iCCP+sRGB / sRGB only / iCCP only; `read_end` into a separate end-info struct |\n\nRuntime **0.42 s**; stable over 8 repeat runs (both parallel and `--test-threads=1`). 15 distinct C warning strings are exercised.\n\n## Things I had to work around (not translation bugs)\n\n1. **`target/cbuild/libpng.so` is not linked against libm** (`ldd` shows only libz/libc) but `png_fixed_ITU`/`png_set_sCAL` call `floor` → `symbol lookup error: undefined symbol: floor`. Fixed by `dlopen(\"libm.so.6\", RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL)` before the first call (the harness `pair()` gained the identical workaround while I was working; my copy is idempotent and keeps the file self-contained).\n2. **`tests/support/core.rs` disagrees with `png.h`** on several constants, so I defined correct ones locally (I did not edit `core.rs`): `PNG_INFO_cICP` 0x40000 vs **0x20000**, `PNG_INFO_cLLI` 0x80000 vs **0x40000**, `PNG_INFO_mDCV` 0x100000 vs **0x80000**, `PNG_FREE_ROWS` 0x0020 vs **0x0040**, `PNG_FREE_TEXT` 0x0200 vs **0x4000**, `PNG_FREE_UNKN` 0x0800 vs **0x0200**, `PNG_FREE_ALL` 0x7FFF vs **0xFFFF**. Consequence: `log_all_info`'s `valid.cICP/cLLI/mDCV` lines are mislabelled (they read the neighbouring flags) — harmless for differential comparison but worth fixing. Also `Core::set_mDCV_fixed`/`get_mDCV_fixed` type the chromaticities as `u32` whereas `png.h` uses `png_fixed_point` (`i32`); I resolve my own correctly-typed pointers.\n3. **`png_get_IHDR` re-runs `png_check_IHDR`**, so calling `log_all_info` on a virgin `png_create_info_struct` raises `png_error(\"Invalid IHDR data\")`. C24's end-info struct therefore gets a valid IHDR before `png_read_end`.\n4. **Real indeterminism in C22**: `png_read_png` allocates row buffers with `png_malloc` (uninitialised) and `png_combine_row` *preserves the padding bits of the final partial byte from the destination buffer*. For 1/2/4-bit rows whose width is not a whole number of bytes this made `row0` differ (`07` vs `08`) purely from heap garbage. Fixed by installing the harness' zero-filling allocator via `png_set_mem_fn` before `png_read_png` — the significant bits and the written byte stream are still compared exactly.\n\n## C behaviours the tests pin down (identical in both libraries)\n\n* **`hIST` can never survive a read in this fork.** `pngrutil.c`'s ordering table has `CDhIST … hPLTE, hIHDR` i.e. `pos_before = PNG_HAVE_PLTE`, so `png_handle_chunk` rejects hIST once PLTE has been seen — yet `png_write_info` emits hIST *after* PLTE. Every hIST read yields `WARNING(hIST: out of place)`. Looks like an upstream/fork bug; the Rust translation reproduces it exactly.\n* `iCCP` profiles of 132/136/144 bytes are rejected on read with `iCCP: too short` (compressed payload < `LZ77Min`); 256 B and up round-trip fully, profile bytes included.\n* `pCAL` only round-trips for (type, nparams) ∈ {(0,2),(1,3),(2,3),(3,4)}; all other counts give `pCAL: invalid parameter count` on read.\n* `PLTE` on a greyscale image is refused on write (`Ignoring request to write a PLTE chunk in grayscale PNG`).\n\n## Note on files touched\n\nI ran `rustfmt tests/chunks.rs`, which recursively reformatted `tests/support/mod.rs` and `tests/support/pngbuild.rs`. I restored both: `pngbuild.rs` is byte-exact again (10209 B; verified in both directions — my 3 reverts hit the original size exactly and re-running rustfmt reproduces the formatted size), and `mod.rs` is the original bytes plus the `ensure_libm` helper that the harness owner had added in the meantime (28525 + 741 = 29266 B). `core.rs` and `testshim.c` were untouched. Nothing in `src/`, `c_src/`, `Cargo.toml` or other test files was modified.","usage":{"total_tokens":403489,"tool_uses":166,"duration_ms":2620077},"uuid":"759647c7-291c-4fba-93a3-4030735d94f7","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e"}
