{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a4b316eba349d9208","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SAzHAkNEUsfGnGttcLZctZ","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-4DaaTZ-translated-rust/11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e/tasks/a4b316eba349d9208.output","summary":"Created `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust/tests/read_b.rs` (2113 lines, 17 `#[test]` fns `r17_…`–`r33_…`, rows R17–R33). Nothing else was touched.\n\n## Per-test result\n\n| fn | result |\n|---|---|\n| `r17_set_shift` | **pass** — all 15 ct/bd × interlace 0/1 × with/without sBIT × 3 random `PngColor8` shift sets; plus shift+expand+packing on sBIT+tRNS inputs; plus a 1-byte palette sBIT (\"bad length\" benign error) |\n| `r18_set_gamma` | **FAIL — genuine translation bug (process abort), details below.** All non-sBIT configurations (9 ct/bd × {no gAMA, gAMA 0.45455, gAMA 1.0} × 5 float pairs + 11 fixed-point pairs incl. flag values `-1`/`-2`, `PNG_LIB_GAMMA_MIN/MAX` and their off-by-one neighbours, `0`, `i32::MAX`) pass |\n| `r19_alpha_mode` | pass — 4 modes × 3 float + 3 fixed output gammas × 8 ct/bd × gAMA present/absent, both `_fixed` and float entry points, plus tRNS+expand variants |\n| `r20_background` | pass — 4 gamma codes × need_expand 0/1 × gamma on/off × float/fixed × 10 ct/bd, plus expand+gamma composite variants, plus 4 background colours (2 random, all-zero, legal max) |\n| `r21_quantize` | pass — full_quantize 0/1 × max_colors {2,4,16,100,256} × NULL/random `u16` histogram × palette inputs (image's own PLTE) and RGB/RGBA inputs (32- and 256-entry caller palette) × interlaced × `png_set_quantize` called twice; logs `png_get_PLTE`, the caller palette after the call, and all rows |\n| `r22_user_transform` | pass — callback logs all `PngRowInfo` fields + row in/out and rewrites the row; 15 ct/bd × interlace × {none, expand, gray_to_rgb, both}; `png_set_user_transform_info` with 5 depth/channel pairs × NULL/non-NULL ptr, logging `png_get_user_transform_ptr` and `png_get_rowbytes`; plus the \"info change after png_read_update_info\" app-error path |\n| `r23_read_status_fn` | pass — `(row,pass)` callback over `png_read_row`, `png_read_rows` (whole pass and 1 row), `png_read_image`, interlace 0/1, all ct/bd + extra shapes 1×1, 9×8, 17×3 |\n| `r24_crc_action` | pass — all 6×6 crit/ancil combinations on 6 streams (clean RGB, clean palette, bad-CRC tEXt, IDAT, IHDR, PLTE); one `diff` run per combination |\n| `r25_unknown_chunks` | pass — keep ∈ {0,1,2,3,−1} × chunk_list {NULL with num 0/−1/2, and lists of 0/1/2/3/4 names} on palette and RGB streams carrying safe-to-copy and unsafe private chunks before PLTE, before IDAT and after IDAT; `png_handle_as_unknown` over 30 names + NULL; `png_set_read_user_chunk_fn` returning −1/0/1 × 4 keep values × NULL/non-NULL user ptr, logging name/size/loc/data and `png_get_user_chunk_ptr` |\n| `r26_user_limits` | pass — 7 dimension limit pairs (max, above, exact, narrow, short, tiny, zero) × 2 inputs, 7 chunk-cache values, 6 chunk-malloc values, one `diff` run each; all four getters logged |\n| `r27_sig_bytes` | pass — n = 0..8 with the first n signature bytes removed, all 15 ct/bd; plus n = 1..7 with the signature left intact |\n| `r28_start_read_image` | pass — 6 sequences (update_info; start_read_image; update_info ×2; neither; start_read_image ×2; update_info then start_read_image) × 3 transform sets × 15 ct/bd × interlace; the C duplicate-call errors are preserved in the trace |\n| `r29_read_end` | pass — end_info struct vs NULL, streams with tEXt/tIME/unknown after IDAT, garbage after IEND, and bare streams, with and without `keep_unknown=ALWAYS`; `log_all_info` on the end-info struct |\n| `r30_transform_stacking` | pass — full pipeline A (expand+gray_to_rgb+add_alpha+swap+bgr+strip_16), pipeline B (…+scale_16+swap_alpha) and 8 seeded random subsets × 15 ct/bd × interlace × tRNS |\n| `r31_create_read_struct_2` | pass — `cb_malloc`/`cb_free` + `trace_alloc` enabled after create+longjmp+create_info; 15 ct/bd × interlace, 5 transform variants, and an unknown-chunk stream; every allocation size/order, `live_allocs` and `malloc_count` compared |\n| `r32_io_state` | pass — own read callback (installed over the harness one, `Core` reached through a `thread_local` raw pointer) logs `png_get_io_state`/`png_get_io_chunk_type` per read; polled again per row and after `read_end`; all ct/bd, unknown-chunk, tEXt+tIME and multi-IDAT streams |\n| `r33_current_row_pass` | pass — polled after every `png_read_row` for interlace 0/1 × 15 ct/bd × shapes 1×1, 5×5, 9×8, plus transform variants |\n\nRuntime: ~7 s total (individually timed), far under the 90 s budget.\n\n## The divergence (R18)\n\n**Configuration** (first hit, `tests/read_b.rs:523`): `R18sbit ct=0 bd=16 sBIT=1 v=0` — a 16-bit image with an sBIT chunk whose significant-bit count is **≤ 8**, gAMA 0.45455 in the stream, `png_set_gamma(png, 1.8, 2.2)` (total correction 3.96, i.e. gamma-significant). Reproduced for colour types 0, 2, 4 and 6 and for every `sBIT ∈ {1,4,8}`; `sBIT ∈ {9,12,16}` matches exactly.\n\n`png_build_gamma_table` (`c_src/src/png.c`) sets `gamma_shift = min(16 - sig_bit, 8)`, so any `sig_bit ≤ 8` yields `gamma_shift == 8`.\n\n```\nC   : p0r0=f923cc70bb4e7949…            (minimal 2x1 ct=4 sBIT=8 repro)\nRUST: thread panicked at src/pngrtran.rs:3497:37:\n      attempt to shift right with overflow   -> SIGABRT\n```\n\nCause: `*sp.offset(1) >> gamma_shift` where `*sp.offset(1)` is `u8`. C promotes `png_byte` to `int`, so `sp[1] >> 8 == 0` (correct: the table has exactly one sub-table). Rust panics in debug; with `overflow-checks = false` (the release profile) the shift amount is masked to `8 & 7 == 0`, so it would silently index `gamma_16_table[sp[1]]` — out of bounds and wrong output. So this is a real correctness bug, not only a debug-assertion artifact.\n\nAffected sites, all the same expression: `src/pngrtran.rs:3349` (RGB), `:3390` (RGB_ALPHA), `:3426` (GRAY_ALPHA), `:3497` (GRAY), and the same pattern in the compose path at `:2846` and `:2936`.\n\nBecause the panic crosses the `extern \"C\"` boundary in the harness trampoline it is non-unwinding and aborts the test process, so `cargo test --test read_b` ends in SIGABRT and the four tests scheduled after `r18` (`r19`, `r20`, `r21`, `r30`) do not get to print their result in that run — each was verified to pass when run on its own (`cargo test --test read_b r19_` etc.). Per instructions the configuration was kept as-is, not weakened and not ignored; a comment above the loop records the bug.\n\nTwo things worth noting about test-side pitfalls I found and corrected while writing this (not library bugs): passing a `png_color_16` background with components > 0xff together with `need_expand == 0` makes the **C** library index its 256-entry `gamma_table` out of bounds, so R20's \"max\" background is capped at 0xff for 8-bit-sample inputs; and `png_set_user_transform_info` is only used with non-increasing depth/channels, since a larger pixel depth makes libpng copy more bytes out of `row_buf` than it holds.","usage":{"total_tokens":266078,"tool_uses":88,"duration_ms":1459204},"uuid":"db2b5f22-39d0-4b5e-95ad-867c14f31308","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e"}
