rth recording (all reproduced identically by the Rust port)\n1. **Transform setters must be called after `png_write_info`.** `png_set_IHDR` (pngset.c:435) does *not* populate `png_ptr->bit_depth/color_type/usr_bit_depth/usr_channels`; `png_write_IHDR` (pngwutil.c:812-827) does. `png_set_swap`/`packing`/`packswap`/`shift`/`filler` all validate against those fields, so W17/W22 apply them after `png_write_info` — exactly the order `png_write_png` uses.\n2. **`png_set_compression_buffer_size` order of checks** (pngset.c:1797): the `zowner != 0` test precedes the `size < 6` test, so after the first row it *always* warns \"cannot be changed because it is in use\" regardless of size. Setting it after `png_write_info` but before the first row still takes effect (IDAT deflate is only claimed by the first `png_compress_IDAT`).\n3. **Two `png_write_flush` calls with no row data in between are fatal.** zlib returns `Z_BUF_ERROR` (`avail_in==0 && RANK(flush) <= RANK(old_flush)`), and `png_compress_IDAT`'s else-branch calls `png_error(… \"buffer error\")`. This is reached on interlaced images where most rows of a pass are skipped. W14 keeps these configurations and tolerates the longjmp (the truncated stream + `rc` are still compared); the purely automatic-flush modes are still required to complete with `rc == 0`.\n4. **Adam7 + trailing `png_write_flush` quirk:** after the last pass `png_write_finish_row` leaves `row_number == 0` while `num_rows == height`, so a `png_write_flush` after all rows is *not* the documented no-op — it re-claims the deflate stream and calls the flush callback. Reproduced identically.\n5. **`png_get_IHDR` re-runs `png_check_IHDR`**, so it png_errors on a second (end-)info struct that never saw `png_set_IHDR`. W21 therefore logs tIME/text explicitly instead of `log_all_info` for the end info.\n6. **`num_palette_max` is 0 in a freshly created write struct**, so out-of-range-index checking is on by default; `png_set_check_for_invalid_index(png, allowed<=0)` disables it. Because `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` is not configured, `\"Wrote palette index exceeding num_palette\"` is a **fatal** error on write — W24 asserts `rc != 0` exactly when `allowed > 0 && the rows overflow`.\n7. **W23 / `png_struct` size:** with `trace_alloc` enabled before `png_create_write_struct_2`, the first allocation differs legitimately (C `MALLOC(#1,1232)` vs Rust `MALLOC(#1,1224)`) — this is the documented internal-layout difference. Everything after it matches, including `png_info` (so the test enables `trace_alloc` after `create_write_struct_2` + `png_set_longjmp_fn` but *before* `png_create_info_struct`, which is stricter than required), all row/filter/zlib allocation sizes and order, the free order, and `live_allocs == 0` at the end."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6974,"cache_read_input_tokens":296594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6974,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0142wgcwC4DU2gkmXGMTmwBC","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"605cd6b9-2cc6-44d5-8d25-f2fd3f8a642d","timestamp":"2026-08-14T16:08:38.593Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write write_b tests W13-W24"}
