{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ccjaif6tdz6af3itgdjcd2p7cix23dduw5fryze7vzwldindpoxq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust/tests/simplified.rs` (2136 lines, 7 `#[test]` fns, whole file runs in 2.4 s). Nothing else was touched.\n\n## Results\n\n| test fn | result |\n|---|---|\n| `s1_read_srgb_formats` | **pass** |\n| `s2_read_linear_formats` | **pass** |\n| `s3_read_colormap_formats` | **fail** (one root cause, below) |\n| `s4_background_and_negative_stride` | **fail** (same) |\n| `s5_write_to_memory` | **fail** (same) |\n| `s6_file_and_stdio` | **fail** (same) |\n| `s7_image_free` | **fail** (same) |\n\nEach test fn is ordered so all contract-satisfying configurations run *before* a clearly marked error-path block, so everything ahead of the reported divergence is verified as byte-identical. No test was weakened, ignored or removed.\n\n## One genuine translation bug — all 5 failures\n\n`png_safe_execute` (`src/pngerror.rs:591`) never sees the `longjmp` from `png_safe_error`, because `setjmp` is called inside a *helper function* in `csupport/shim.c`:\n\n```c\nint png_rust_setjmp(jmp_buf *env) { return setjmp(*env); }\n```\n\n`setjmp` must execute in the frame that `longjmp` is meant to resume; wrapping it means the saved frame is dead when the `longjmp` happens (UB). Observable effect: **after any `png_error` caught by `png_safe_execute`, the Rust build returns 1 (success) where C returns 0.** `warning_or_error` (=2) and `message` are still set correctly, so `PNG_IMAGE_FAILED()` happens to work, but the documented return value is wrong; sometimes Rust also keeps executing past the error (different message, bytes written) or skips `png_image_free` (leak). Fix would be to give the shim a callback form so the `setjmp` frame stays live — exactly like `th_protect` in `tests/support/testshim.c`.\n\n### Exact traces / triggering configurations\n\n* **S3e / S4e** `ct=0 bd=1 il=0 tRNS out=RGB_COLORMAP nobg` — 5×3 GRAY/1-bit + tRNS; `begin` identical (rc=1, fmt=0x1, cmap_entries=2); then `format=PNG_FORMAT_RGB_COLORMAP`, `background=NULL`, stride=5, colormap 6 bytes:\n  * C : `finish rc=0` woe=2 msg=`\"background color must be supplied to remove alpha/transparency\"`\n  * RUST: `finish rc=1` woe=2 msg=`\"bad color-map processing (internal error)\"`\n  Affects every RGB/BGR_COLORMAP output with an alpha- or tRNS-bearing input and `background==NULL`.\n* **S5e** `fmt=RGB stride_too_small=17` — `png_image_write_to_memory(w=6,h=4,PNG_FORMAT_RGB, memory=NULL, row_stride=17)`:\n  * C : `query rc=0 memory_bytes=0` msg=`\"supplied row stride too small\"`\n  * RUST: `query rc=1 memory_bytes=0`, same msg (and the follow-up real write also returns 1 with 0 bytes).\n  Same for `\"no color-map for color-mapped image\"` and `\"png_write_image: unsupported transformation\"` (there Rust even reports `memory_bytes=46`, i.e. it kept writing).\n* **S6notpng** `png_image_begin_read_from_file` on an existing 39-byte non-PNG:\n  * C : `rc=0 opaque_null=1` msg=`\"Not a PNG file\"`\n  * RUST: `rc=1 opaque_null=0` msg=`\"Not a PNG file\"` (also leaks `png_control`/`png_struct`).\n* **S7b** truncated IDAT (last 24 bytes cut): C `finish rc=0` / RUST `finish rc=1`, msg `\"read beyond end of data\"` in both. Same for S7c (cut IHDR — `begin` itself: C 0 / Rust 1, opaque left non-NULL), S7g (failed write) and every `S7 cut=N`.\n\n### Independent confirmation of blast radius\n\nWith a standalone C `dlopen` harness I swept **9120 read** configurations (15 colour-type/bit-depth combos × interlace × 19 output formats × background/negative-stride/padding) and **816 write** configurations against both `.so`s: exactly 304 read + 236 write configurations diverge and **every one** has the signature \"C returns 0, Rust returns 1\" on a `png_error` path. **Zero divergences on any success path** — all decoded buffers, colour maps, slack bytes and produced PNG byte streams match exactly.\n\n### What the passing coverage includes\nAll 15 legal (colour_type, bit_depth) combos × interlace 0/1 × shapes 1×1…17×3 × the 9 sRGB, 4 LINEAR and 6 COLORMAP output formats; inputs with tRNS, gAMA, sRGB, cHRM (sRGB-matching and not), cICP, mDCV (both) — i.e. all branches of `png_image_is_not_sRGB`; `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_16BIT_sRGB`; padded and negative (bottom-up) row strides; 4 backgrounds × 10 alpha/tRNS inputs; colour-map contents and `colormap_entries` before/after; `png_image_write_to_memory` size-query → write → too-small → zero-size for every format × `convert_to_8_bit` × colormap entry counts 1…256 × stride variants × `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_{COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB,FAST}`; `write_to_file`/`write_to_stdio`/`begin_read_from_file`/`begin_read_from_stdio` round trips through real temp files (distinct per `lib.tag`, file contents compared as hex); and all direct argument-validation paths (`invalid argument`, `incorrect PNG_IMAGE_VERSION`, `strerror(ENOENT)`, NULL image/name/FILE). All `PNG_IMAGE_*` macros are reimplemented as Rust fns and every buffer carries 64 bytes of separately-logged slack."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":601,"cache_read_input_tokens":259826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":601,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Q6KZeTob5KWmg2bn2G4oMT","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"56f81eae-6f21-4442-9a25-1e514e462ca6","timestamp":"2026-08-14T16:11:11.640Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write simplified API tests S1-S7"}
