{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jxsrq3kqrqhmbe2cotckvibmrk5afwht27zxsec4u3vfhbx7wqkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Final state verified. Here is the report.\n\n## What was created\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust/tests/progressive.rs` (1503 lines, only file touched) — 8 `#[test]` fns, ~5100 differential configurations, each driving both `.so`s over byte-identical input and comparing the full trace.\n\nEvery read struct is built with `png_create_read_struct_2` + the harness `cb_malloc`/`cb_free` (which `calloc`), because the progressive row callback exposes `png_struct::row_buf` directly (the columns before `PNG_PASS_START_COL(pass)` of an expanded interlaced row are never written by libpng); zeroed allocations make that deterministic in both libraries. Info/row/end/user-chunk callbacks reach the current library's function table through a `thread_local` raw pointer to a `#[repr(C)] Ctx`.\n\n## Per-test result\n\n| test | configs | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `p1_feed_sizes_all_combos` | 1413 | **pass** |\n| `p2_interlaced_combine` | 1350 | **pass** |\n| `p3_process_data_pause` | 688 pass, then **FAIL (abort)** | genuine divergence, see below |\n| `p4_process_data_skip` | 144 | **pass** |\n| `p5_transforms_in_info_callback` | 405 | **pass** |\n| `p6_multi_idat` | 358 | **pass** |\n| `p7_ancillary_and_unknown_chunks` | 394 | **pass** |\n| `p8_progressive_ptr` | 24 | **pass** |\n\n`timeout 600 cargo build && timeout 600 cargo test --test progressive -- --skip p3_` → 7 passed in 1.3 s. `cargo test --test progressive` (including p3) dies with SIGABRT inside the Rust `.so`.\n\n## The divergence (p3, section (d))\n\nTriggering configuration: `P3r ct=0 bd=8 il=0 save=0 at=1` — 5x5 8-bit grey, non-interlaced, 98-byte file fed to `png_process_data` in **one** call, with `png_process_data_pause(png, 0)` called from inside the **first row callback** (the documented use; the docs only require the call to be inside `png_process_data`).\n\n* **C**: `PAUSE(row,save=0)=57`, then the reader finishes the current IDAT chunk, delivers all 5 rows, fires the end callback, `rc=0`, 113 trace lines, `live_allocs=0`.\n* **Rust**: `thread panicked at src/pngpread.rs:483:9: attempt to subtract with overflow` → `thread caused non-unwinding panic. aborting.` → SIGABRT (no trace at all).\n\nCause: `png_process_data_pause` sets `buffer_size = 0` while `png_push_read_IDAT` is still inside `png_process_IDAT_data`; on return it executes `png_ptr->buffer_size -= save_size` (`c_src/src/pngpread.c:455` and `:482`). In C that is a defined unsigned wraparound and the read completes correctly. `src/pngpread.rs:454` and `:483` translate it as a plain `-=`, which trips the dev-profile overflow check; the panic crosses the `extern \"C\"` boundary and aborts. `TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md` (\"Use `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub` … to mirror C wraparound\") makes this a translation bug — `wrapping_sub` on both lines. Nothing in `src/` was modified; the test is kept, not ignored, not weakened.\n\nTwo deliberate restrictions in that section, both documented in the file: only the whole-file feed is used (with a partial feed the wrapped `buffer_size` makes the C reader read from an exhausted buffer), and `save = 1` is not used from the row callback (`png_push_save_buffer` also zeroes `current_buffer_size`, so the same subtraction wraps that too and the C reader walks off the end of the caller's buffer — no defined behaviour to compare against).\n\n## Coverage notes\n\n* **P1** feeds 1/2/3/7/13/64/whole x 15 combos x w 1,7,17 x h 1,5 x 2 seeds, plus all five row filters, `png_start_read_image` instead of `png_read_update_info`, non-interlaced `png_progressive_combine_row`, all 8 single-byte signature corruptions, and 8 truncation points.\n* **P2** Adam7, all 15 combos, feeds 1/5/64/whole, 11 shapes chosen to hit every special case of `png_push_process_row` (`height <= 4`, widths making pass 1/3/5 empty), `png_progressive_combine_row` into a persistent image with every intermediate destination row logged, plus the \"no `png_set_interlace_handling`\" mode (raw sub-image rows, exact per-pass byte count).\n* **P3** pause save=0/1 in the info callback (all combos x interlace x 5 feed sizes), with a 600-byte tEXt + 400-byte unknown chunk in the save buffer, and in the **user chunk callback** (a pause exactly at a chunk boundary — that path is well defined for both save values). Pending saved data is resumed with zero-length `png_process_data` calls.\n* **P4** `png_process_data_skip` is *not implemented* in 1.6.59: it calls `png_app_warning`, which by default is `png_error` (longjmp, `rc=1`) and only a warning after `png_set_benign_errors(png,1)`. Both variants tested, before/after every `png_process_data` and after a pause, with 700/900-byte unknown+tEXt chunks before and after IDAT.\n* **P5** 11 transform sets (`expand`, `gray_to_rgb`, `strip_16`, `packing`, `gamma(2.2,0.45455)`, `bgr`, `expand_16`, `swap` and combinations) x 15 combos, non-interlaced and interlaced-with-combine.\n* **P6** IDAT re-split into 1/2/3-byte chunks x zero-length IDAT at start/middle/end/all x interlace x feeds, plus the pngpread.c-only structural checks, which reproduce identically in both libraries: `Missing IHDR before IDAT`, `Missing PLTE before IDAT`, `Not enough compressed data`, `IDAT: Too many IDATs found`, `Extra compressed data in IDAT`, `Extra compression data in IDAT`.\n* **P7** gAMA/cHRM/sBIT/tIME/bKGD/tEXt/zTXt + private chunks before *and* after IDAT x keep AS_DEFAULT/NEVER/IF_SAFE/ALWAYS (global default, per-chunk list naming *known* chunks, and both together) x user chunk callback returning -1/0/1 (name, NUL, size, location and data logged). Reaches `error in user chunk` and the `forcing save of an unhandled chunk` app-error path.\n* **P8** `png_get_progressive_ptr` compared against the passed pointer (boolean only) right after `png_set_progressive_read_fn`, in all three callbacks, with a NULL user pointer, after re-setting the callbacks to NULL, and with a NULL `png_ptr`.\n\n`CONFIGS.md` rows P1..P8 are still unchecked — I was told not to edit any file but `tests/progressive.rs`.\n\nA debug aid is included: `PDUMP=1 cargo test --test progressive <fn> -- --nocapture` dumps every trace with its configuration label and the exact input bytes (`eprintln!` only, never part of the compared trace)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":858,"cache_read_input_tokens":296926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":858,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AxwS3LQDAQG2Gmsh4CrGkB","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"d327ff75-a6cd-404a-bd5c-c6ff179b4baa","timestamp":"2026-08-14T16:15:33.258Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write progressive tests P1-P8"}
