{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01FxnqAD3VanP7gMgTRbVzK9","type":"tool_result","content":"translation.log\n# ERRORS.md — error / rejection surface of the C implementation\n\nDerived **mechanically** from `c_src/src/*.c` (`tmp/gen_errors.py`): every call to an\nerror/warning/report macro, every sentinel `return 0 / NULL / -1` in an *exported*\nfunction, and every `assert`.  One row per distinct rejection site.\n\nSemantics of the \"expected C result\" column (see `pngerror.c`, `pnglibconf.h` —\nthis build has `PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` + `PNG_BENIGN_READ_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`\nbut **not** `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`, and `PNG_ERROR_NUMBERS` is off):\n\n* `png_error` / `png_chunk_error` / `png_fixed_error` — call `error_fn` with the exact\n  message, then `longjmp` (harness returns non-zero `rc`).\n* `png_app_error` — fatal unless `PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN` (set by\n  `png_set_benign_errors(1)`), else a warning.\n* `png_benign_error` / `png_chunk_benign_error` — on a **read** struct: warning when\n  `PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN` is set, otherwise fatal; on a **write** struct always fatal.\n* `png_warning` / `png_app_warning` / `png_chunk_warning` — `warning_fn` with the exact\n  message, execution continues.\n* `png_chunk_report(..., PNG_CHUNK_ERROR|WARNING|WRITE_ERROR)` — dispatches to the above.\n* `png_image_error` — simplified API: stores the message in `image->message`, returns 0.\n* `png_zstream_error` — records a zlib message consumed by a later error/warning.\n\nEvery row is exercised by the Phase C differential tests: both libraries are driven\ninto the condition and the *complete* message/return trace must be byte identical.\nCoverage is verified mechanically by `tests/error_coverage.rs`, which records every\nmessage string emitted by the C library and requires the Rust library to emit the\nidentical sequence (see `ERROR_COVERAGE.md`, regenerated by `tmp/coverage.py`).\n\n| # | function | file:line | trigger (guarding condition in the C source) | rejection | expected C result |\n|---|----------|-----------|----------------------------------------------|-----------|-------------------|\n| 1 | `png_set_sig_bytes` | png.c:66 | `if (nb > 8)` | `png_error(\"Too many bytes for PNG signature\")` | fatal error -> longjmp |\n| 2 | `png_sig_cmp` | png.c:88 | `else if (num_to_check < 1)` | `return` sentinel | returns -1 to the caller |\n| 3 | `png_sig_cmp` | png.c:91 | `if (start > 7)` | `return` sentinel | returns -1 to the caller |\n| 4 | `PNG_FUNCTION` | png.c:120 | `if (size != 0 && items >= (~(png_alloc_size_t)0) / size)` | `png_warning(\"Potential overflow in png_zalloc()\")` | non-fatal warning |\n| 5 | `png_user_version_check` | png.c:245 | `if ((png_ptr->flags & PNG_FLAG_LIBRARY_MISMATCH) != 0)` | `png_warning(\"(no literal message)\")` | non-fatal warning |\n| 6 | `png_user_version_check` | png.c:248 | `(unconditional at this point in the flow)` | `return` sentinel | returns 0 to the caller |\n| 7 | `png_data_freer` | png.c:479 | `else if (freer == PNG_USER_WILL_FREE_DATA)` | `png_error(\"Unknown freer parameter in png_data_freer\")` | fatal error -> longjmp |\n| 8 | `png_get_io_ptr` | png.c:694 | `if (png_ptr == NULL)` | `return` sentinel | returns NULL to the caller |\n| 9 | `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` | png.c:749 | `if (out == NULL)` | `return` sentinel | returns 0 to the caller |\n| 10 | `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` | png.c:756 | `if (ptime->year > 9999 /* RFC1123 limitation */ \\|\\| ptime->month == 0 \\|\\| ptime->month > 12 \\|\\| ptime->day == 0 \\|\\| ptime->day > 31 \\|\\| ptime->hour > 23 \\|\\| ptime->minute > 5` | `return` sentinel | returns 0 to the caller |\n| 11 | `png_convert_to_rfc1123` | png.c:802 | `if (png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer(png_ptr->time_buffer, ptime) == 0)` | `png_warning(\"Ignoring invalid time value\")` | non-fatal warning |\n| 12 | `png_convert_to_rfc1123` | png.c:808 | `if (png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer(png_ptr->time_buffer, ptime) == 0)` | `return` sentinel | returns NULL to the caller |\n| 13 | `(file scope)` | png.c:1003 | `(unconditional at this point in the flow)` | `png_zstream_error(\"(no literal message)\")` | sets zstream->msg for a later png_error/warning |\n| 14 | `png_xy_from_XYZ` | png.c:1199 | `if (png_muldiv(&xy->whitey, whiteY, PNG_FP_1, dwhite) == 0)` | `return` sentinel | returns 0 to the caller |\n| 15 | `png_XYZ_from_xy` | png.c:1495 | `if (png_muldiv(&XYZ->blue_Z, PNG_FP_1 - xy->bluex - xy->bluey, blue_scale, PNG_FP_1) == 0)` | `return` sentinel | returns 0 to the caller |\n| 16 | `(file scope)` | png.c:1539 | `(unconditional at this point in the flow)` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"(no literal message)\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 17 | `png_icc_profile_error` | png.c:1571 | `(unconditional at this point in the flow)` | `png_chunk_benign_error(\"(no literal message)\")` | benign chunk error: warning on read, fatal on write |\n| 18 | `icc_check_length` | png.c:1589 | `if (profile_length < 132)` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"too short\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 19 | `png_icc_check_length` | png.c:1598 | `if (!icc_check_length(png_ptr, name, profile_length))` | `return` sentinel | returns 0 to the caller |\n| 20 | `png_icc_check_length` | png.c:1607 | `if (profile_length > png_chunk_max(png_ptr))` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"profile too long\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 21 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1627 | `if (temp != profile_length)` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"length does not match profile\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 22 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1632 | `if (temp > 3 && (profile_length & 3))` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"invalid length\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 23 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1638 | `if (temp > 357913930 \\|\\| /* (2^32-4-132)/12: maximum possible tag count */ profile_length < 132+12*temp) /* truncated tag table */` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"tag count too large\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 24 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1646 | `if (temp >= 0xffff) /* The ICC limit */` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"invalid rendering intent\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 25 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1653 | `if (temp >= PNG_sRGB_INTENT_LAST)` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"intent outside defined range\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 26 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1670 | `if (temp != 0x61637370)` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"invalid signature\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 27 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1681 | `if (memcmp(profile+68, D50_nCIEXYZ, 12) != 0)` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"PCS illuminant is not D50\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 28 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1709 | `if ((color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) == 0)` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"RGB color space not permitted on grayscale PNG\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 29 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1715 | `if ((color_type & PNG_COLOR_MASK_COLOR) != 0)` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"Gray color space not permitted on RGB PNG\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |\n| 30 | `png_icc_check_header` | png.c:1720 | `default:` | `png_icc_profile_error(\"invalid ICC profile color space\")` | iCCP profile rejected (benign error on read) |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KcmjwwCyBbM1feG2dR297D","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"89d118c2-0194-48e1-a103-464ae26274a5","timestamp":"2026-08-14T16:20:42.338Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Fix C integer-promotion shift bugs"}
