{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3ssexafcmff7qlsdm5pvvqcchivwm6izghbq5kzpmkbdm2vsfqda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Final verification and cleanup are complete. Here is my report.\n\n## What I wrote\n\nOne new file, `tests/err_stream.rs` (2862 lines, 36 `#[test]` fns, whole file runs in **0.38 s**). Every malformed input is its own `diff(...)` run; the C‑vs‑Rust comparison covers messages, warning‑vs‑fatal, longjmp `rc`, partial info state and decoded rows.\n\n| group | tests |\n|---|---|\n| stream/chunk | `signature_and_header`, `chunk_order`, `crc_and_length`, `ancillary_values`, `text_chunks`, `truncation_and_duplicates`, `random_mutations` (seeded delete/duplicate/reorder/truncate/resize/bit‑flip over 5 bases × 24 seeds), `iccp_chunks`, `zlib_stream` |\n| rows | `interlace_and_rows`, `row_depth_checks` |\n| limits/unknown | `limits`, `splt_chunk_cache`, `unknown_chunks` |\n| progressive | `progressive_errors` |\n| memory | `oom_paths` (own read struct via `png_create_read_struct_2` + a size‑triggered failing allocator) |\n| FFI/I-O | `ffi_null_and_range`, `io_functions` |\n| simplified API | `simplified_args`, `simplified_stdio_args`, `simplified_bad_format`, `simplified_plain_read`, `simplified_malformed`, `simplified_cmap_*` (13 fns, one per colour‑map branch) |\n\n## Pass/fail\n\n**22 pass, 14 fail.** All 14 failures are simplified‑API tests and all have **one** root cause (below). Everything else — sequential, progressive, chunk, CRC, zlib, text, iCCP, limits, unknown‑chunk, allocation‑failure, NULL‑pointer and stdio I/O paths — is byte‑identical.\n\n## Worklist coverage: 103 of 134 (77 %)\n\nVerified with a **freshly deleted** `observed_msgs.txt`, so 103 is my file alone (396 distinct C messages). The 31 not triggered, with reasons:\n\n* **19 internal-consistency assertions of the simplified-API engine** (`pngread.c` 1537, 1586, 1643, 1743, 2738, 2761, 2766, 2800, 2803, 2836, 3074, 3159, 3208, 3358, 3361, 3364, 3369, 3382, 3609, 3960, 3986, 3994): they switch on values libpng itself produced (interlace/colour type/bit depth already validated by IHDR; `do_local_background==2` implies exactly the state the checks demand; every `png_create_colormap_entry` call site passes an index ≤ 255; the per-branch “too few entries” test is strictly stronger than the final `color map overflow` test). Undefined `image->format` bits, the only app-controlled route into this area, are caught by `pngread.c:3925`, which **is** triggered.\n* **3 cannot overflow on 64-bit**: `pngpread.c:361` (`save_buffer_size > SIZE_MAX-(current+256)`), `pngrutil.c:1635` (needs > `SIZE_MAX`/10 sPLT entries), `pngrutil.c:4649` (`rowbytes ≤ 2^34`).\n* **1 dead code**: `pngrutil.c:211 \"bad header (invalid length)\"` — `png_read_chunk_header` calls `png_get_uint_31` two lines earlier, so any length with bit 31 set always errors with “PNG unsigned integer out of range” (triggered) first.\n* **4 impossible internal states**: `pngpread.c:378`, `pngpread.c:502` (both call sites guarantee `length>0`/non-NULL, and `png_calculate_crc` would fault first), `pngread.c:1431` (`image->opaque` cannot be NULL while the memory read fn is installed), `pngrutil.c:3255` (`width==0` rejected by IHDR; `pixel_depth==0` is caught by 3243, which **is** triggered).\n* **1 needs a failing system malloc**: `pngread.c:1169` — `png_image_read_init` allocates before any user allocator can be installed (the simplified API has no `png_set_mem_fn` hook).\n\nNewly reached rows that needed non-obvious set-ups: `.Too many IDATs found` / `Too many IDATs found` (keep-unknown IDAT + a second `png_read_info`), `internal row logic error` (`png_progressive_combine_row` from the info callback), `sequential/progressive row overflow` and `internal … row size calculation error` (a user transform that rewrites `row_info` while `png_set_user_transform_info` is *not* used), `internal row size calculation error`, iCCP `extra compressed data` (a valid 144-byte ICC profile plus > 1024 bytes of trailing data so `png_inflate_read` never consumes it), the OOM rows (size-triggered allocator: 999/`len`/10000/505/777 and 257 for `Insufficient memory for save_buffer`).\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**One genuine translation defect, 14 failing tests.** In the C, `png_safe_execute` (pngerror.c:820) executes `setjmp(safe_jmpbuf)` **in its own frame**. The Rust port (`src/pngerror.rs:591`) calls `setjmp_shim(&mut safe_jmpbuf)`, which is `csupport/shim.c`’s `png_rust_setjmp(jmp_buf *env){ return setjmp(*env); }` — the saved context belongs to a helper frame that is dead by the time `png_safe_error` (`src/pngerror.rs:552`) does `longjmp(error_buf, 1)`. The observable effect is that **the Rust simplified API does not catch `png_error`: the guarded function appears to have succeeded.** Examples (first divergent trace line, `rc` = the value returned by the libpng entry point):\n\n```\n[SIMG truncated 8]   C: (read beyond end of data) rc=0 … opaque=0\n                  RUST: (read beyond end of data) rc=1 … opaque=1\n[SIMG cmap gray8]    C: (gray[8] color-map: too few entries) rc=0\n                  RUST: (gray[8] color-map: too few entries) rc=1\n[SIMG cmap rgb]      C: (rgb color-map: too few entries) rc=0\n                  RUST: (bad color-map processing (internal error)) rc=1\n```\n\nSo `png_image_begin_read_from_memory` / `png_image_finish_read` return **success** after a fatal error (and leave `image->opaque` allocated), and execution resuming on the dead frame sometimes carries on into later stages, producing a *different* message (`bad color-map processing (internal error)`). An application checking only the return value would use an unfilled buffer. `src/png.rs:238` uses the identical `setjmp_shim` pattern inside `png_create_read_struct_2`, so the version-check longjmp path is likely affected the same way.\n\nNo other divergence exists: notably the failing-allocator runs pass, which proves both libraries request the same allocation sizes at the same points.\n\n**Two upstream C NULL-deref traps** (not divergences, but I excluded them from the NULL-argument matrix after the reference `.so` segfaulted): `png_process_data_skip(NULL)` (pngpread.c:92 — no NULL check, `png_app_warning` dereferences `png_ptr`) and `png_get_io_state(NULL)`. Both are documented in comments in the test file.\n\nI did not touch anything besides `tests/err_stream.rs` (I only re-appended the pre-existing lines to the generated `target/testsupport/observed_msgs.txt` after deleting it for an exact coverage measurement)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_read_input_tokens":484120,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":855,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01466Nqb5z9B7fwBv76vVDfC","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"6ff90c33-da82-4a5c-b993-5d9742aed8b3","timestamp":"2026-08-14T16:27:49.409Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase C read-stream error tests"}
