ide `png_create_read_struct_2`, so the version-check longjmp path is likely affected the same way.\n\nNo other divergence exists: notably the failing-allocator runs pass, which proves both libraries request the same allocation sizes at the same points.\n\n**Two upstream C NULL-deref traps** (not divergences, but I excluded them from the NULL-argument matrix after the reference `.so` segfaulted): `png_process_data_skip(NULL)` (pngpread.c:92 — no NULL check, `png_app_warning` dereferences `png_ptr`) and `png_get_io_state(NULL)`. Both are documented in comments in the test file.\n\nI did not touch anything besides `tests/err_stream.rs` (I only re-appended the pre-existing lines to the generated `target/testsupport/observed_msgs.txt` after deleting it for an exact coverage measurement).","usage":{"total_tokens":486501,"tool_uses":122,"duration_ms":2479219},"uuid":"e3af2293-de10-4bee-987c-85c5c7fffeeb","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e"}
