{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a3122e0c5bef28d9f","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Tj9Vx55RTNVxwYcjTcZuak","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-4DaaTZ-translated-rust/11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e/tasks/a3122e0c5bef28d9f.output","summary":"Done. `src/pngpread.rs` is the only file changed (6 statements, in 2 blocks).\n\n## 1. Sites changed\n\n| Rust site | Mirrors C | Operand types | Input condition that makes it wrap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/pngpread.rs:458` `idat_size` | `pngpread.c:453` | `png_uint_32 -= png_uint_32` | **Cannot actually wrap** — the local `idat_size` is `min(png_ptr->idat_size, save_size)`. Converted because §1 explicitly directed it; `wrapping_sub` is value-identical when no wrap occurs. |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:459` `buffer_size` | `pngpread.c:455` | `size_t -= size_t` | Row callback calls `png_process_data_pause(png, 0)` (or `1`) during `png_process_IDAT_data`; that sets `buffer_size = 0`, so `0 - save_size` wraps. |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:460` `save_buffer_size` | `pngpread.c:456` | `size_t -= size_t` | Only via `pause(save=1)` → `png_push_save_buffer()` reshuffles the save buffer; `save_size` stays ≤ the (grown) `save_buffer_size`, so no wrap observed — converted for symmetry with the C statement. |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:490` `idat_size` | `pngpread.c:480` | `png_uint_32 -= png_uint_32` | Same as row 1 — cannot wrap. |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:491` `buffer_size` | `pngpread.c:482` | `size_t -= size_t` | **This was the reported live abort.** `pause` from the first row callback → `buffer_size = 0` → `0 - save_size`. |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:492` `current_buffer_size` | `pngpread.c:483` | `size_t -= size_t` | `pause(save=1)` from the row callback → `png_push_save_buffer()` sets `current_buffer_size = 0` → `0 - save_size` wraps. |\n\n## 2. Audit method and result\n\nBeyond reading the C for every `-=`/`-`/`+=`/`*` candidate in all 26 `src/*.rs` files (~330 sites), I made the audit **empirical**: I built `c_src` a second time with `clang -fsanitize=unsigned-integer-overflow` (into a throwaway `target/ubsan`, since `c_src/` is read-only) and ran (a) the whole differential suite and (b) a purpose-built ~330-line C driver (progressive reads with all 6 pause/skip callback positions × 9 feed sizes, truncations, byte mutations, 24 read-transform combos, all colour-type/bit-depth/interlace combos, write-side transforms and filters, `png_ascii_from_fp` edge values, simplified API with negative strides) against it. That yields the exact set of places the C *actually* relies on unsigned wraparound:\n\n| C wrap site | Rust status |\n|---|---|\n| `pngpread.c:481,482` (`buffer_size`, `current_buffer_size`) | **the bug — now fixed** |\n| `pngpread.c:165` (`num_to_check - 4` in `png_push_read_sig`) | already `wrapping_sub` |\n| `pngrutil.c:167,173` (`check_chunk_name` SWAR `name -= PNG_U32(...)`) | already `wrapping_sub` |\n| `png.c:2405,2590` (`czero = 0U-exp_b10`, `uexp_b10 = 0U-exp_b10`) | already `wrapping_sub` |\n| `pngread.c:4114`, `pngwrite.c:2033` (`check = -(png_uint_32)row_stride`) | already `wrapping_neg` |\n\nI then rebuilt the same driver against the **Rust** cdylib (dev profile, `overflow-checks` on) and ran the identical workload for **23 minutes: zero panics, zero aborts**. No further conversions were needed.\n\n**Examined and deliberately left checked** (the guard makes wrapping unreachable, so the check is a useful assertion): `png_push_fill_buffer` `buffer_size/save_buffer_size/current_buffer_size -= save_size` (reachable only after `buffer_size` has already wrapped *up*); `png_crc_finish` `skip -= len`; `png_inflate`/`png_inflate_read`/`png_decompress_chunk` `*output_size_ptr`/`*input_size_ptr`/`*chunk_bytes`/`*out_size`/`limit` (all clamped first); `user_chunk_cache_max -= 1` (guarded by `!= 0` + `== 1`); iCCP/iTXt/sPLT/PLTE `length -= read_length`, `read_length -= keyword_length+2`, `length - 3*num`, `length - prefix_length` (all length-checked); every `row_width -= bytes_to_jump` / `c -= 2|4` in `png_combine_row` and `png_do_read_interlace`; `optimize_cmf` `z_cinfo -= 1` and `png_deflate_claim` `window_bits -= 1` (window bits clamped to 8..15 by `png_set_compression_window_bits`); all `shift -= 1|2|4` packing loops (reset at 0); Paeth filter `p = b - c` (signed `int`); `255 - alpha`, `256 - v`, `7 - (x & 7)` families; all `size_t`/`usize` multiplications (`png_rowbytes`, `width * channels`, array sizings) which are 64-bit and bounded by `PNG_UINT_31_MAX`; `png_ascii_from_fp`'s `size -= 1` chain (sized by the `size >= precision+5` precondition); `png_fp_add`/`png_fp_sub`/`png_XYZ_from_xy` (signed, range-checked). Two spots are *theoretically* wrappable in C but require an impossible allocation and behave identically to C: `png_push_save_buffer`'s `PNG_SIZE_MAX - (current_buffer_size + 256)`, and `png_write_pCAL`'s `total_len += params_len[i]`.\n\n## 3. Verification\n\n- `cargo build` — clean (3 pre-existing unused-import warnings).\n- `cargo test --test progressive` — **8 passed, 0 failed**, including `p3_process_data_pause`; no SIGABRT.\n- `lowlevel_a/lowlevel_b/read_a/read_b/write_a/write_b/chunks/smoke` — **133 passed, 0 failed** (24/18/30/16/17/4/12/12), identical to the pre-change baseline.\n\nNote for the record (not caused by this change, and not in the verification set): `tests/simplified.rs` (14 failures) and `tests/err_stream.rs` (5 failures) fail identically before and after, with the untouched reference `libpng.so` — pre-existing translation divergences elsewhere. All temporary artifacts (`target/ubsan`, the fuzz driver) were removed and `target/cbuild/libpng.so` was restored byte-identical; nothing under `c_src/` or `tests/` was touched.","usage":{"total_tokens":197345,"tool_uses":142,"duration_ms":2385910},"uuid":"750ef8ac-3e3b-4b73-9b48-2274c0bc08b7","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e"}
