esult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are fixing a systematic C→Rust translation bug class in a libpng 1.6.59 translation.\n\nWorking dir: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust`\nNever modify anything under `c_src/` (ground truth) or under `tests/`.\n\n## The bug class: unsigned wraparound translated as a checked operation\n\nC unsigned arithmetic wraps. The translation used plain `-=` / `+=` / `*` on unsigned Rust\nintegers, which **panics** under the dev profile (`overflow-checks` on) and, in release\n(`overflow-checks = false`), wraps — but a panic that crosses the `extern \"C\"` boundary is\nnon-unwinding and ABORTS the whole process, so the library is unusable in a debug build and any\ndivergence is masked in release.\n\nConfirmed live failure (differential test `tests/progressive.rs::p3_process_data_pause`):\n\n```\nConfig: 5x5 8-bit grey PNG, whole 98-byte file in ONE png_process_data call, with\n        png_process_data_pause(png, 0) called from inside the first row callback.\nC   : PAUSE(row,save=0)=57, reader finishes the IDAT, delivers all 5 rows, rc=0\nRUST: thread panicked at src/pngpread.rs:483:9:\n      attempt to subtract with overflow -> non-unwinding panic -> SIGABRT\n```\nCause: `png_process_data_pause` sets `png_ptr->buffer_size = 0` while\n`png_push_read_IDAT` is still inside `png_process_IDAT_data`; on return the C executes\n`png_ptr->buffer_size -= save_size` (`c_src/src/pngpread.c:455` and `:482`) which legitimately\nwraps around, and the read still completes correctly. The Rust translation at\n`src/pngpread.rs:454` and `src/pngpread.rs:483` uses a plain `-=`.\n\n## Task\n\n### 1. Fix the two reported sites\n\nIn `src/pngpread.rs`, the statements mirroring `c_src/src/pngpread.c:453-457` and `:480-484`:\n```rust\n(*png_ptr).idat_size -= idat_size;\n(*png_ptr).buffer_size -= save_size;\n(*png_ptr).save_buffer_size -= save_size;      // resp. current_buffer_size\n```\nEvery one of those C statements is unsigned arithmetic that may wrap when the application called\n`png_process_data_pause`. Translate each as `wrapping_sub` (keeping the exact same operand types),\ne.g.\n```rust\n(*png_ptr).buffer_size = (*png_ptr).buffer_size.wrapping_sub(save_size);\n```\nCheck the C types first (`c_src/include/pngstruct.h`: `buffer_size`, `save_buffer_size`,\n`current_buffer_size` are `size_t`, `idat_size` is `png_uint_32`) and keep the Rust field types\nuntouched — only the operation changes.\n\n### 2. Audit the WHOLE crate for the same class\n\nGo through every `src/*.rs` file (they are 1:1 translations: `src/pngpread.rs` ↔\n`c_src/src/pngpread.c`, `src/pngrutil_a1.rs`/`_a2`/`_b1a`/`_b1b`/`_b2` ↔ `c_src/src/pngrutil.c`,\n`src/png.rs` ↔ `png.c`, and so on) and find every arithmetic operation on an UNSIGNED integer\nthat can underflow/overflow for some input the public API accepts:\n\n```bash\ngrep -rnE \"[-+*]=|[^=<>!+-]\\+[^+=]|[^=<>!+-]-[^->=]\" src/*.rs | wc -l   # then work through it\n```\nFocus on (a) `-=` and `a - b` on `size_t`/`png_uint_32`/`png_alloc_size_t`/`u8`/`u16`,\n(b) `+=`/`+`/`*` that can exceed the type's range, (c) any counter/length bookkeeping that a\n`png_error`, a `pause`, a `skip`, a zero-length chunk, a truncated stream or a user callback can\ndrive out of range.\n\nFor each candidate: read the corresponding C statement, decide whether the C can actually reach a\nwrapping value, and if so convert it to the explicit `wrapping_*` form. **Do not** convert\noperations that provably cannot wrap (leave them checked — that is a useful assertion), and never\nchange the VALUE that a non-wrapping case produces.\n\nPrioritise the modules the differential tests drive hardest, in this order:\n`pngpread.rs`, `pngrutil_a1.rs`, `pngrutil_a2.rs`, `pngrutil_b1b.rs`, `pngrutil_b2.rs`,\n`pngread.rs`, `pngwutil.rs`, `pngwrite.rs`, `pngrtran.rs`, `pngtrans.rs`, `pngwtran.rs`,\n`png.rs`, `pngmem.rs`, `pngset.rs`, `pngget.rs`, `pngerror.rs`.\n\n### 3. Verify\n\n```bash\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo build 2>&1 | tail -3\ntimeout 600 cargo test --test progressive 2>&1 | tail -25          # all 8 must pass, no SIGABRT\ntimeout 600 cargo test --test lowlevel_a --test lowlevel_b --test read_a --test read_b \\\n    --test write_a --test write_b --test chunks --test smoke 2>&1 | grep -E \"test result|FAILED|error\\[\"\n```\n`cargo test` does NOT rebuild the cdylib — always `cargo build` first.\n`progressive` MUST fully pass (in particular `p3_process_data_pause`), and no previously passing\ntest may break. Do not touch `tests/` or `c_src/`; do not \"fix\" a test.\n\nFINAL REPORT: a table of every site you changed (file:line, the C line it mirrors, operand types,\nthe input condition that makes it wrap), a summary of the candidates you examined and left checked,\nand the test results.","agentId":"a3122e0c5bef28d9f","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `src/pngpread.rs` is the only file changed (6 statements, in 2 blocks).\n\n## 1. Sites changed\n\n| Rust site | Mirrors C | Operand types | Input condition that makes it wrap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/pngpread.rs:458` `idat_size` | `pngpread.c:453` | `png_uint_32 -= png_uint_32` | **Cannot actually wrap** — the local `idat_size` is `min(png_ptr->idat_size, save_size)`. Converted because §1 explicitly directed it; `wrapping_sub` is value-identical when no wrap occurs. |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:459` `buffer_size` | `pngpread.c:455` | `size_t -= size_t` | Row callback calls `png_process_data_pause(png, 0)` (or `1`) during `png_process_IDAT_data`; that sets `buffer_size = 0`, so `0 - save_size` wraps. |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:460` `save_buffer_size` | `pngpread.c:456` | `size_t -= size_t` | Only via `pause(save=1)` → `png_push_save_buffer()` reshuffles the save buffer; `save_size` stays ≤ the (grown) `save_buffer_size`, so no wrap observed — converted for symmetry with the C statement. |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:490` `id