{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"af5ef800648495d74","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_015Wr4KZtzCqFrc5zUk9fgdS","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-4DaaTZ-translated-rust/11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e/tasks/af5ef800648495d74.output","summary":"Fixed. The `setjmp` pad now lives in a C frame that is alive for the whole protected region, so `longjmp` lands correctly.\n\n## New shim — `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust/csupport/shim.c`\n\n`png_rust_setjmp` was deleted (nothing else used it) and replaced by a callback-based pad:\n\n```c\nint png_rust_protect(void **env_slot, int (*body)(void *), void *arg,\n    int on_longjmp)\n{\n    jmp_buf env;\n\n    if (setjmp(env) == 0)\n    {\n        *env_slot = (void *)env;  /* jmp_buf is an array type: decays */\n        return body(arg);\n    }\n\n    return on_longjmp;\n}\n```\n\nNo parameter is modified after `setjmp`, so their values are well defined on the longjmp return path without `volatile`. One shim function sufficed for both call sites, so no second variant was added. `build.rs` needed no change.\n\n`src/cffi.rs`: the `setjmp_shim` extern was replaced by\n`png_rust_protect(env_slot: *mut *mut c_void, body: Option<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void) -> c_int>, arg: *mut c_void, on_longjmp: c_int) -> c_int`\n— `body`'s type is exactly `png_safe_execute`'s `function` type, so it is passed straight through with no transmute.\n\n## `png_safe_execute` — `src/pngerror.rs`\n\n`env_slot` is `&mut image->opaque->error_buf` itself (types match exactly: `*mut png_voidp`), so the shim performs the C assignment `image->opaque->error_buf = safe_jmpbuf` at exactly the same point C does, inside the `setjmp == 0` branch:\n\n```rust\nlet saved_error_buf = (*(*image).opaque).error_buf;      // BEFORE the pad is installed\nlet result = png_rust_protect(\n    core::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*(*image).opaque).error_buf),\n    function, arg, 0 /* on longjmp: failure */);\n(*(*image).opaque).error_buf = saved_error_buf;          // always restored\nif result != 0 { return 1; }                             // success\nif saved_error_buf.is_null() { png_image_free(image); }\n0\n```\n\nC restores `error_buf` twice on the normal path (idempotent), so restoring once after the shim returns is semantically identical; the longjmp path and the `result == 0` path both fall through to the free-and-return-0 tail exactly as in `c_src/src/pngerror.c:815-848`.\n\n## `png_create_png_struct` — `src/png.rs`\n\nThe `if (!setjmp(create_jmp_buf))` block became a C-ABI body function plus a `#[repr(C)]` context (no `Drop` fields; a longjmp skips destructors):\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\nstruct png_create_struct_ctx {\n    pad: *mut c_void,               // written by the shim = C's &create_jmp_buf\n    create_struct: *mut png_struct_def,\n    user_png_ver: png_const_charp,\n    png_ptr: png_structp,           // carries the result out (body returns int)\n}\n```\n\n`env_slot` is `addr_of_mut!((*ctx).pad)` (a real `*mut *mut c_void`, avoiding any type-punned write into the `*mut jmp_buf` field), and the body's first act is `(*create_struct).jmp_buf_ptr = (*ctx).pad as *mut jmp_buf; jmp_buf_size = 0; longjmp_fn = Some(longjmp);` — the same three assignments, in the same order, as the C. `*png_ptr = create_struct` is now `copy_nonoverlapping(create_struct, png_ptr, 1)` since `create_struct` is reached through a pointer. Body returns 1 (with `ctx.png_ptr` set) only at C's \"successful return point\"; version-check failure, malloc failure and the longjmp path all yield `NULL`. The struct init (`user_*_max`, `png_set_mem_fn`, `png_set_error_fn`) stays before the pad is installed, as in C.\n\n## Test results (all in `target/debug`, after `cargo build`)\n\n| test file | result |\n|---|---|\n| simplified | 7 passed / 0 failed (was 5 failing) |\n| err_stream | 36 passed / 0 failed (was 14 failing) |\n| chunks | 24 / 0 |\n| lowlevel_a | 18 / 0 |\n| lowlevel_b | 30 / 0 |\n| progressive | 8 / 0 |\n| read_a | 16 / 0 |\n| read_b | 17 / 0 |\n| write_a | 12 / 0 |\n| write_b | 12 / 0 |\n| smoke | 4 / 0 |\n\n184 tests, 0 failures, nothing regressed. Also verified under `cargo build --release` + `cargo test --release --test simplified --test err_stream` (7/7 and 36/36), confirming the fix is not optimization-fragile. Only the three pre-existing unused-import warnings remain; nothing under `tests/` or `c_src/` was touched.","usage":{"total_tokens":53525,"tool_uses":31,"duration_ms":317650},"uuid":"eed16d12-9f92-4256-bf18-690c74855b61","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_015Wr4KZtzCqFrc5zUk9fgdS","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The `setjmp` pad now lives in a C frame that is alive for the whole protected region, so `longjmp` lands correctly.\n\n## New shim — `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust/csupport/shim.c`\n\n`png_rust_setjmp` was deleted (nothing else used it) and replaced by a callback-based pad:\n\n```c\nint png_rust_protect(void **env_slot, int (*body)(void *), void *arg,\n    int on_longjmp)\n{\n    jmp_buf env;\n\n    if (setjmp(env) == 0)\n    {\n        *env_slot = (void *)env;  /* jmp_buf is an array type: decays */\n        return body(arg);\n    }\n\n    return on_longjmp;\n}\n```\n\nNo parameter is modified after `setjmp`, so their values are well defined on the longjmp return path without `volatile`. One shim function sufficed for both call sites, so no second variant was added. `build.rs` needed no change.\n\n`src/cffi.rs`: the `setjmp_shim` extern was replaced by\n`png_rust_protect(env_slot: *mut *mut c_void, body: Option<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void) -> c_int>, arg: *mut c_void, on_longjmp: c_int) -> c_int`\n— `body`'s type is exactly `png_safe_execute`'s `function` type, so it is passed straight through with no transmute.\n\n## `png_safe_execute` — `src/pngerror.rs`\n\n`env_slot` is `&mut image->opaque->error_buf` itself (types match exactly: `*mut png_voidp`), so the shim performs the C assignment `image->opaque->error_buf = safe_jmpbuf` at exactly the same point C does, inside the `setjmp == 0` branch:\n\n```rust\nlet saved_error_buf = (*(*image).opaque).error_buf;      // BEFORE the pad is installed\nlet result = png_rust_protect(\n    core::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*(*image).opaque).error_buf),\n    function, arg, 0 /* on longjmp: failure */);\n(*(*image).opaque).error_buf = saved_error_buf;          // always restored\nif result != 0 { return 1; }                             // success\nif saved_error_buf.is_null() { png_image_free(image); }\n0\n```\n\nC restores `error_buf` twice on the normal path (idempotent), so restoring once after the shim returns is semantically identical; the longjmp path and the `result == 0` path both fall through to the free-and-return-0 tail exactly as in `c_src/src/pngerror.c:815-848`.\n\n## `png_create_png_struct` — `src/png.rs`\n\nThe `if (!setjmp(create_jmp_buf))` block became a C-ABI body function plus a `#[repr(C)]` context (no `Drop` fields; a longjmp skips destructors):\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\nstruct png_create_struct_ctx {\n    pad: *mut c_void,               // written by the shim = C's &create_jmp_buf\n    create_struct: *mut png_struct_def,\n    user_png_ver: png_const_charp,\n    png_ptr: png_structp,           // carries the result out (body returns int)\n}\n```\n\n`env_slot` is `addr_of_mut!((*ctx).pad)` (a real `*mut *mut c_void`, avoiding any type-punned write into the `*mut jmp_buf` field), and the body's first act is `(*create_struct).jmp_buf_ptr = (*ctx).pad as *mut jmp_buf; jmp_buf_size = 0; longjmp_fn = Some(longjmp);` — the same three assignments, in the same order, as the C. `*png_ptr = create_struct` is now `copy_nonoverlapping(create_struct, png_ptr, 1)` since `create_struct` is reached through a pointer. Body returns 1 (with `ctx.png_ptr` set) only at C's \"successful return point\"; version-check failure, malloc failure and the longjmp path all yield `NULL`. The struct init (`user_*_max`, `png_set_mem_fn`, `png_set_error_fn`) stays before the pad is installed, as in C.\n\n## Test results (all in `target/debug`, after `cargo build`)\n\n| test file | result |\n|---|---|\n| simplified | 7 passed / 0 failed (was 5 failing) |\n| err_stream | 36 passed / 0 failed (was 14 failing) |\n| chunks | 24 / 0 |\n| lowlevel_a | 18 / 0 |\n| lowlevel_b | 30 / 0 |\n| progressive | 8 / 0 |\n| read_a | 16 / 0 |\n| read_b | 17 / 0 |\n| write_a | 12 / 0 |\n| write_b | 12 / 0 |\n| smoke | 4 / 0 |\n\n184 tests, 0 failures, nothing regressed. Also verified under `cargo build --release` + `cargo test --release --test simplified --test err_stream` (7/7 and 36/36), confirming the fix is not optimization-fragile. Only the three pre-existing unused-import warnings remain; nothing under `tests/` or `c_src/` was touched."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: af5ef800648495d74 (use SendMessage with to: 'af5ef800648495d74', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 55059\ntool_uses: 31\nduration_ms: 317651</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"ed66b7e9-0df0-49b7-8887-dc25757f41cf","timestamp":"2026-08-14T17:09:52.086Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are fixing a real translation defect in a libpng 1.6.59 C→Rust translation.\n\nWorking dir: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust`\nNever modify anything under `c_src/` (ground truth) and never modify anything under `tests/`.\nYou MAY modify `csupport/shim.c`, `build.rs`, `src/cffi.rs`, `src/pngerror.rs`, `src/png.rs`.\n\n## The defect\n\n`setjmp` must be executed in the stack frame that the later `longjmp` is supposed to resume.\nThe translation calls it through a helper:\n\n```c\n/* csupport/shim.c */\nint png_rust_setjmp(jmp_buf *env) { return setjmp(*env); }\n```\nso the context saved in `env` belongs to `png_rust_setjmp`'s own frame, which is dead by the time\nthe `longjmp` happens. Two call sites use it:\n\n* `src/pngerror.rs:600` in `png_safe_execute` (mirrors `c_src/src/pngerror.c:815-848`, where the\n  `setjmp(safe_jmpbuf)` is in `png_safe_execute`'s own frame). The matching `longjmp` is in\n  `png_safe_error` (`src/pngerror.rs`, mirroring `pngerror.c`).\n* `src/png.rs:238` in the version-check path (mirrors `c_src/src/png.c` `png_create_png_struct`'s\n  `setjmp(create_jmp_buf)`), whose `longjmp` comes from `png_error` while the struct is being\n  created.\n\nConfirmed live consequences (differential tests, both C and Rust loaded through `dlopen`):\n\n```\ntests/simplified.rs  : 5 tests fail   (304 read + 236 write configurations)\ntests/err_stream.rs  : 14 tests fail\nSignature of EVERY failure: after a png_error inside the simplified API,\n   C   returns 0 (failure) and leaves image->opaque == NULL,\n   RUST returns 1 (success) and leaves image->opaque allocated,\nand sometimes Rust keeps executing past the error so a LATER, different message is reported:\n   [SIMG cmap rgb]  C: (rgb color-map: too few entries) rc=0\n                 RUST: (bad color-map processing (internal error)) rc=1\n   [SIMG truncated 8] C: (read beyond end of data) rc=0 opaque_null=1\n                 RUST: (read beyond end of data) rc=1 opaque_null=0\n```\nThere are ZERO divergences on the success paths, so the ONLY thing wrong is that the\n`longjmp` does not land correctly.\n\n## Required fix\n\nRestructure the shim so that the frame performing `setjmp` is the frame that stays alive, i.e.\npass the body as a callback. Suggested shape (adapt as needed, keep it minimal and C89-clean):\n\n```c\n/* csupport/shim.c */\n#include <setjmp.h>\n\n/* Run body(arg) with a setjmp landing pad whose address is published through\n * *env_slot (exactly what C libpng does when it stores `safe_jmpbuf` in\n * image->opaque->error_buf).  Returns body's return value, or `on_longjmp`\n * if a longjmp to the pad occurred.\n */\nint png_rust_protect(void **env_slot, int (*body)(void *), void *arg, int on_longjmp)\n{\n    jmp_buf env;\n    if (setjmp(env) == 0)\n    {\n        *env_slot = (void *)env;      /* jmp_buf is an array type: decays to a pointer */\n        return body(arg);\n    }\n    return on_longjmp;\n}\n```\nThen rewrite `png_safe_execute` in `src/pngerror.rs` to use it while preserving the C semantics\nEXACTLY (read the C at `c_src/src/pngerror.c:815-848` again):\n\n* `saved_error_buf = image->opaque->error_buf` captured BEFORE the pad is installed;\n* on the normal path: `error_buf = <pad>`, `result = function(arg)`,\n  `error_buf = saved_error_buf`, and `return 1` when `result != 0`;\n* on the longjmp path and on `result == 0`: `error_buf = saved_error_buf`, then\n  `if (saved_error_buf == NULL) png_image_free(image);` and `return 0`.\n\nThe Rust `function` argument is `Option<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(png_voidp) -> c_int>`, which is\nABI-compatible with the C `int (*)(void*)` the shim expects, so you can pass it straight through\n(transmute the `Option<fn>` to the raw pointer if the types need help). The body closure must not\nown anything needing `Drop` — a longjmp skips destructors.\n\nApply the same treatment to the `src/png.rs:238` site: study `png_create_png_struct` in\n`c_src/src/png.c` to see exactly which state must be restored, then express it with\n`png_rust_protect` so the pad lives in the right frame. If that site needs a slightly different\nsignature (e.g. it stores the buffer in `png_ptr->jmp_buf_ptr`/`jmp_buf_local` rather than a\n`void*` slot), add a second small shim function rather than distorting the first.\n\nKeep the old `png_rust_setjmp` only if something still needs it; otherwise remove it and its\n`extern` declaration in `src/cffi.rs`. `build.rs` already compiles `csupport/shim.c` into a static\nlib that the cdylib links — check whether it needs any change (it should not).\n\nWatch out for one thing: whatever you store in `error_buf` / `jmp_buf_ptr` must remain valid for\nas long as libpng may `longjmp` to it, i.e. for the whole duration of `body(arg)`. Storing the\naddress of the shim's own `jmp_buf` (as above) is correct because the shim frame is alive for\nexactly that period.\n\n## Verify\n\n```bash\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo build 2>&1 | tail -3\ntimeout 900 cargo test --test simplified 2>&1 | tail -30      # all 7 must pass\ntimeout 900 cargo test --test err_stream 2>&1 | tail -40      # all 36 must pass\ntimeout 900 cargo test --test lowlevel_a --test lowlevel_b --test read_a --test read_b \\\n  --test write_a --test write_b --test chunks --test progressive --test smoke 2>&1 \\\n  | grep -E \"test result|FAILED|error\\[\"\n```\n`cargo test` does NOT rebuild the cdylib — always `cargo build` first.\nNo previously passing test may break. Do not modify anything under `tests/` or `c_src/`, and do not\nweaken or ignore a test.\n\nFINAL REPORT: the new shim source, the rewritten `png_safe_execute` and the `src/png.rs` change,\nplus the full test results (per test file: passed/failed). If any simplified/err_stream test still\nfails, give the exact remaining divergence.","agentId":"af5ef800648495d74","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The `setjmp` pad now lives in a C frame that is alive for the whole protected region, so `longjmp` lands correctly.\n\n## New shim — `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/translated_rust/csupport/shim.c`\n\n`png_rust_setjmp` was deleted (nothing else used it) and replaced by a callback-based pad:\n\n```c\nint png_rust_protect(void **env_slot, int (*body)(void *), void *arg,\n    int on_longjmp)\n{\n    jmp_buf env;\n\n    if (setjmp(env) == 0)\n    {\n        *env_slot = (void *)env;  /* jmp_buf is an array type: decays */\n        return body(arg);\n    }\n\n    return on_longjmp;\n}\n```\n\nNo parameter is modified after `setjmp`, so their values are well defined on the longjmp return path without `volatile`. One shim function sufficed for both call sites, so no second variant was added. `build.rs` needed no change.\n\n`src/cffi.rs`: the `setjmp_shim` extern was replaced by\n`png_rust_protect(env_slot: *mut *mut c_void, body: Option<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void) -> c_int>, arg: *mut c_void, on_longjmp: c_int) -> c_int`\n— `body`'s type is exactly `png_safe_execute`'s `function` type, so it is passed straight through with no transmute.\n\n## `png_safe_execute` — `src/pngerror.rs`\n\n`env_slot` is `&mut image->opaque->error_buf` itself (types match exactly: `*mut png_voidp`), so the shim performs the C assignment `image->opaque->error_buf = safe_jmpbuf` at exactly the same point C does, inside the `setjmp == 0` branch:\n\n```rust\nlet saved_error_buf = (*(*image).opaque).error_buf;      // BEFORE the pad is installed\nlet result = png_rust_protect(\n    core::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*(*image).opaque).error_buf),\n    function, arg, 0 /* on longjmp: failure */);\n(*(*image).opaque).error_buf = saved_error_buf;          // always restored\nif result != 0 { return 1; }                             // success\nif saved_error_buf.is_null() { png_image_free(image); }\n0\n```\n\nC restores `error_buf` twice on the normal path (idempotent), so restoring once after the shim returns is semantically identical; the longjmp path and the `result == 0` path both fall through to the free-and-return-0 tail exactly as in `c_src/src/pngerror.c:815-848`.\n\n## `png_create_png_struct` — `src/png.rs`\n\nThe `if (!setjmp(create_jmp_buf))` block became a C-ABI body function plus a `#[repr(C)]` context (no `Drop` fields; a longjmp skips destructors):\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\nstruct png_create_struct_ctx {\n    pad: *mut c_void,               // written by the shim = C's &create_jmp_buf\n    create_struct: *mut png_struct_def,\n    user_png_ver: png_const_charp,\n    png_ptr: png_structp,           // carries the result out (body returns int)\n}\n```\n\n`env_slot` is `addr_of_mut!((*ctx).pad)` (a real `*mut *mut c_void`, avoiding any type-punned write into the `*mut jmp_buf` field), and the body's first act is `(*create_struct).jmp_buf_ptr = (*ctx).pad as *mut jmp_buf; jmp_buf_size = 0; longjmp_fn = Some(longjmp);` — the same three assignments, in the same order, as the C. `*png_ptr = create_struct` is now `copy_nonoverlapping(create_struct, png_ptr, 1)` since `create_struct` is reached through a pointer. Body returns 1 (with `ctx.png_ptr` set) only at C's \"successful return point\"; version-check failure, malloc failure and the longjmp path all yield `NULL`. The struct init (`user_*_max`, `png_set_mem_fn`, `png_set_error_fn`) stays before the pad is installed, as in C.\n\n## Test results (all in `target/debug`, after `cargo build`)\n\n| test file | result |\n|---|---|\n| simplified | 7 passed / 0 failed (was 5 failing) |\n| err_stream | 36 passed / 0 failed (was 14 failing) |\n| chunks | 24 / 0 |\n| lowlevel_a | 18 / 0 |\n| lowlevel_b | 30 / 0 |\n| progressive | 8 / 0 |\n| read_a | 16 / 0 |\n| read_b | 17 / 0 |\n| write_a | 12 / 0 |\n| write_b | 12 / 0 |\n| smoke | 4 / 0 |\n\n184 tests, 0 failures, nothing regressed. Also verified under `cargo build --release` + `cargo test --release --test simplified --test err_stream` (7/7 and 36/36), confirming the fix is not optimization-fragile. Only the three pre-existing unused-import warnings remain; nothing under `tests/` or `c_src/` was touched."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":317651,"totalTokens":55059,"totalToolUseCount":31,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1272,"cache_read_input_tokens":51941,"output_tokens":1844,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":74},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1272},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":2,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":25,"editFileCount":4,"linesAdded":185,"linesRemoved":74,"otherToolCount":0}}}
