o`, after `png_write_end`, more rows than\n  `height`, `png_write_image` with NULL row pointers, `png_write_rows` with num_rows > remaining,\n  `png_write_end` without any row, `png_write_info` twice, `png_write_info` after rows,\n  `png_write_png` without `png_set_rows`, interlaced write without\n  `png_set_interlace_handling`, writing 0 rows then `png_write_end`\n* palette: `png_set_PLTE` with num_palette 0, -1, 257, > (1<<bit_depth); PLTE missing for colour\n  type 3; PLTE on greyscale; `png_set_tRNS` with num_trans out of range; palette index >=\n  num_palette in a row (`png_do_check_palette_indexes`)\n* text: keyword empty / > 79 chars / with control characters / leading-trailing spaces; NULL text\n  with a compression method that needs it; invalid `compression` values (e.g. -2, 3, 99);\n  iTXt without lang/lang_key; text that fails to compress\n* iCCP/sPLT: invalid keyword, profile length 0/too short/mismatched, `png_set_sPLT` with\n  nentries 0/negative, depth other than 8/16\n* other chunk setters that validate on write: `png_set_sBIT` out of range, `png_set_bKGD` index\n  out of range, `png_set_hIST` without PLTE, `png_set_pCAL` bad equation type / param count,\n  `png_set_sCAL_s` with a non-numeric or empty string, `png_set_sCAL` with 0/negative,\n  `png_set_pHYs`/`png_set_oFFs` invalid unit, `png_set_cICP` invalid matrix,\n  `png_set_eXIf_1` with length < 4, `png_set_unknown_chunks` with an invalid name / bad location,\n  `png_set_gAMA` 0 or out of range, `png_set_sRGB` intent > 3, `png_set_cHRM` out of range\n* manual chunk writers: `png_write_chunk_start` with a huge length, `png_write_chunk_data` with\n  NULL data or more data than declared, `png_write_chunk_end` without a start, an invalid chunk\n  name (non-alphabetic bytes)\n* compression settings: `png_set_compression_level` out of range (-2, 10),\n  `png_set_compression_method` != 8, `png_set_compression_window_bits` < 8 / > 15,\n  `png_set_compression_mem_level` out of range, `png_set_compression_buffer_size` < 6 and while\n  in use, the same for all four `png_set_text_compression_*`\n* write transforms applied to the wrong colour type (`png_set_filler`, `png_set_swap`,\n  `png_set_packing`, `png_set_packswap`, `png_set_shift` without/with bad sBIT,\n  `png_set_invert_alpha`, `png_set_swap_alpha` — these produce app errors/warnings), and\n  `png_write_png` with a read-only transform bit\n* I/O failure: make the write callback fail — `with_session(|s| s.write_limit = Some(n))` makes\n  `cb_write` longjmp once n bytes were written; sweep n over several values so the failure lands in\n  the signature, in IHDR, in the middle of IDAT and in IEND. Also `png_write_flush` misuse.\n* OOM: build the struct with `png_create_write_struct_2` + the harness `cb_malloc`/`cb_free` and\n  `with_session(|s| s.malloc_limit = Some(k))`, sweeping k from 0 to ~40 so EVERY internal\n  allocation fails in turn (this is the systematic way to cover the \"Out of Memory\"/\n  \"Insufficient memory\" rows). Compare the full traces including the allocation trace\n  (`s.trace_alloc = true`, enabled AFTER the struct is created — `sizeof(png_struct)` differs\n  legitimately between the two libraries).\n* FFI boundary: NULL `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` to every `png_write_*` and `png_set_*` you touch;\n  out-of-range enum values for `png_set_filter` (method 1, 64, -1; filters 0x07, 0xFF),\n  `png_set_flush(-1)`, `png_set_check_for_invalid_index(-1)`, `png_set_option` invalid,\n  `png_permit_mng_features` with unknown bits.\n\n## Rules\n\n* Use `diff(...)` for every input; a test passes when C and Rust behave identically, INCLUDING\n  when both reject.\n* If they differ, KEEP the test as written, do NOT weaken it, do NOT `#[ignore]`, do NOT modify\n  `src/`. Report it precisely.\n* Never log a pointer/address — only null-ness, sizes, contents. Fixed seeds only.\n* Do NOT edit anything except your new `tests/err_write.rs`.\n* **`cargo test` does NOT rebuild the cdylib.** Always\n  `timeout 600 cargo build && timeout 600 cargo test --test err_write 2>&1 | tail -40`.\n* Runtime under ~120 s.\n\n## Self-check before reporting\n\n```bash\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ\npython3 - <<'EOF'\ntodo=[l.split('| \"')[1].rstrip('\"\\n') for l in open('tmp/todo2_write.txt') if '| \"' in l]\nobs=open('translated_rust/target/testsupport/observed_msgs.txt').read()\nmiss=[t for t in todo if t and t.split('  ')[0] not in obs]\nprint('triggered', len(todo)-len(miss), 'of', len(todo)); print('\\n'.join(miss))\nEOF\n```\nIterate until the missing list contains only rows you can justify as unreachable through the public\nAPI (say why for each). Aim for ≥ 85 %.\n\nFINAL REPORT: test fns + pass/fail, the coverage number, the justified-unreachable list, and every\nC-vs-Rust divergence found, precisely.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-4DaaTZ-translated-rust/11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e/tasks/af7ffd9120d57b0b3.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
