alid\n  matrix coefficient, `png_set_mDCV`/`_fixed` and `png_set_cLLI`/`_fixed` out of range\n* other `pngset.c` validation: `png_set_PLTE` num_palette out of range, `png_set_tRNS` num_trans\n  out of range, `png_set_sBIT` values 0 / > bit_depth, `png_set_hIST` without a palette,\n  `png_set_pCAL` bad equation type / negative nparams, `png_set_sCAL`/`_fixed`/`_s` with\n  0/negative/non-numeric, `png_set_pHYs`/`png_set_oFFs` bad unit, `png_set_eXIf_1` too short,\n  `png_set_text` with a bad keyword / bad compression value, `png_set_sPLT` bad depth/nentries,\n  `png_set_unknown_chunks` with an invalid chunk name and with `num_unknowns` 0/negative,\n  `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` with an out-of-range location, `png_set_rows` with NULL,\n  `png_set_invalid`/`png_get_valid` with an undefined flag bit, `png_data_freer` with an unknown\n  freer value, `png_free_data` with an unknown mask\n* getters with bad state: every `png_get_*` on a NULL png_ptr, on a NULL info_ptr, and on an info\n  struct where the chunk was never set (they must return 0 identically), `png_get_rowbytes`\n  before IHDR, `png_get_IHDR` on an uninitialised info struct (it re-runs `png_check_IHDR`),\n  `png_get_uint_31` with a value >= 2^31, `png_get_int_32` with the \"broken\" 0x80000000 encoding\n* transform setup (`pngrtran.c`/`pngtrans.c`): every setter called at the WRONG time (after\n  `png_read_update_info` / after the first row / on a write struct where it is read-only and vice\n  versa) and with an invalid argument: `png_set_background` with a NULL colour and with\n  background_gamma_code out of range (-1, 4, 99), `png_set_alpha_mode` with mode < 0 / > 3,\n  `png_set_gamma` with 0 / negative, `png_set_rgb_to_gray` with error_action 0/4/99 and\n  coefficients that sum > 1 or are negative, `png_set_quantize` with num_palette 0/-1,\n  maximum_colors 0/1/257, a NULL palette, `png_set_filler` on the wrong colour type,\n  `png_set_shift` with all-zero / out-of-range shifts, `png_set_expand_gray_1_2_4_to_8` on the\n  wrong type, `png_set_scale_16` + `png_set_strip_16` together, `png_set_read_user_transform_fn`\n  on a write struct, `png_set_user_transform_info` with negative depth/channels,\n  `png_set_crc_action` with out-of-range actions, `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` with keep < -1 or\n  > 3 and with a chunk list containing an invalid name, `png_set_interlace_handling` on a\n  non-interlaced image\n* memory API: `png_malloc` with size 0 and with a huge size (fatal \"Out of Memory\"),\n  `png_malloc_warn`/`png_calloc`/`png_malloc_base` with a huge size, `png_free` with NULL,\n  `png_malloc_array`/`png_realloc_array` with negative/huge counts, `png_zalloc` overflow\n  (\"Potential overflow in png_zalloc()\"), and the `png_create_*_struct_2` allocation-failure path\n  via `with_session(|s| s.malloc_limit = Some(k))` for k = 0..5\n* Generic FFI boundary sweep: for EVERY function you touch, also call it with a NULL first\n  argument, and pass out-of-range values for every `int` parameter that the C compares against a\n  fixed set (C enums accept any int).\n  CAUTION: two upstream C functions genuinely dereference NULL (`png_process_data_skip(NULL)` and\n  `png_get_io_state(NULL)`) and would segfault the test process — skip those two, with a comment.\n\n## Rules\n\n* Use `diff(...)` for every input; a test passes when C and Rust behave identically, INCLUDING when\n  both reject. Compare state after the rejection too (log the relevant getters).\n* If they differ, KEEP the test, do NOT weaken it, do NOT `#[ignore]`, do NOT modify `src/`.\n  Report it precisely.\n* Never log a pointer/address — only null-ness, sizes, contents. Fixed seeds only.\n* Do NOT edit anything except your new `tests/err_api.rs`.\n* **`cargo test` does NOT rebuild the cdylib.** Always\n  `timeout 600 cargo build && timeout 600 cargo test --test err_api 2>&1 | tail -40`.\n* Runtime under ~120 s.\n\n## Self-check before reporting\n\n```bash\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4DaaTZ\npython3 - <<'EOF'\ntodo=[l.split('| \"')[1].rstrip('\"\\n') for l in open('tmp/todo2_api.txt') if '| \"' in l]\nobs=open('translated_rust/target/testsupport/observed_msgs.txt').read()\nmiss=[t for t in todo if t and t.split('  ')[0] not in obs]\nprint('triggered', len(todo)-len(miss), 'of', len(todo)); print('\\n'.join(miss))\nEOF\n```\nIterate until the missing list contains only rows you can justify as unreachable through the public\nAPI (give the reason for each). Aim for ≥ 85 %.\n\nFINAL REPORT: test fns + pass/fail, the coverage number, the justified-unreachable list, and every\nC-vs-Rust divergence found, precisely."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3565,"cache_read_input_tokens":358484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3565,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"fd51f21e-5c53-4c93-885d-efa095d0a50c","timestamp":"2026-08-14T17:11:52.179Z"}
