{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DtLvkFr6V1ELQuQ6TALSBe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md — configuration surface (valid inputs) of the C implementation\n2\t\n3\tDerived from the branch structure of `c_src/src/*.c` and the public/internal API\n4\tsurface (`png.h`: 218 `PNG_EXPORT` + 40 `PNG_FP/FIXED_EXPORT` entry points;\n5\t`pngpriv.h`: 184 `PNG_INTERNAL_FUNCTION` entry points — **all** of them are\n6\texported from the `.so` and therefore all of them are directly callable).\n7\t\n8\tThe axes below are the ones the C code actually branches on:\n9\t\n10\t| axis | values the C distinguishes | where |\n11\t|------|----------------------------|-------|\n12\t| colour type | 0 GRAY, 2 RGB, 3 PALETTE, 4 GRAY_ALPHA, 6 RGB_ALPHA | `png_check_IHDR`, `png_read_start_row`, all row transforms |\n13\t| bit depth | 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 (legal subset per colour type) | `png_check_IHDR`, `PNG_ROWBYTES`, sub-byte packing paths |\n14\t| interlace | 0 none, 1 Adam7 (7 passes, per-pass geometry) | `png_do_read_interlace`, `png_do_write_interlace`, `png_combine_row` |\n15\t| width/height | 1 (degenerate), small (sub-byte remainder), > 1 row buffer | `PNG_ROWBYTES` rounding, pass emptiness |\n16\t| filter set | NONE / SUB / UP / AVG / PAETH / ALL, per-row heuristic | `png_write_find_filter`, `png_read_filter_row` |\n17\t| zlib params | level 0/1/6/9, strategy, window bits 8..15, mem level 1..9, method | `png_write_IDAT`, `png_deflate_claim` |\n18\t| IDAT buffering | `png_set_compression_buffer_size`, multi-IDAT split | `png_compress_IDAT` |\n19\t| write API | `png_write_row` / `png_write_rows` / `png_write_image` / `png_write_png` | `pngwrite.c` |\n20\t| read API | sequential (`png_read_row/rows/image/png`) / progressive (`png_process_data`) / simplified (`png_image_*`) | `pngread.c`, `pngpread.c` |\n21\t| read transforms | the 26 `png_ptr->transformations` bits | `pngrtran.c` |\n22\t| flush | `png_set_flush(n)` + `png_write_flush` | `png_write_row` |\n23\t| ancillary chunks | every chunk in `PNG_KNOWN_CHUNKS` (24) + unknown chunks | `pngset.c`, `pngwutil.c`, `pngrutil.c` |\n24\t| unknown handling | AS_DEFAULT / NEVER / IF_SAFE / ALWAYS, per-chunk list, user chunk callback | `png_handle_unknown` |\n25\t| CRC action | DEFAULT / ERROR_QUIT / WARN_DISCARD / WARN_USE / QUIET_USE / NO_CHANGE, critical vs ancillary | `png_crc_finish`, `png_crc_error` |\n26\t| limits | user width/height max, chunk cache max, chunk malloc max | `png_check_IHDR`, `png_handle_unknown` |\n27\t| memory | default vs `png_create_*_struct_2` user malloc/free | `pngmem.c` |\n28\t| number format | float (`png_set_gAMA`) vs fixed (`png_set_gAMA_fixed`) entry points | `pngset.c` |\n29\t\n30\tEach row below is exercised by a differential test that drives **both** `.so`s\n31\tthrough the identical call sequence with pseudo-random (fixed-seed) data and\n32\tcompares the complete trace — return values, every warning/error message, the\n33\tproduced byte stream and every decoded row — byte for byte.\n34\t\n35\t## L — lowest-level entry points (called directly, no png_struct state)\n36\t\n37\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n38\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n39\t| L1 | `png_get_uint_32`, `png_get_uint_16`, `png_get_int_32` | 512 random 4-byte buffers + all boundary patterns (0, 0x7fffffff, 0x80000000, 0xffffffff) | [x] |\n40\t| L2 | `png_get_uint_31` | valid values < 2^31 (read struct present) | [x] |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01XHdnyMuFEuHb5xLVMQCDix","session_id":"11547ad3-7cdc-4bcb-a504-9e6a5631306e","uuid":"7f4b4e25-94e9-4f43-b743-778ef9381523","timestamp":"2026-08-14T17:12:52.369Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Cross-cutting modes tests M1-M8"}
